    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e0e0ac80fe4e283b3d5d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Service graph metrics](https://grafana.com/docs/tempo/latest/metrics-from-traces/service_graphs/) focus on inter-service communication and dependency health. They measure the calls between services, helping Grafana to infer the service topology. However, they measure only the interaction between two services—they don’t include the internal processing time of the client service.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Alerting on span metrics"
      ],
      "source": {
