    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fb0ad5d2640bf324d69c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Divides failed spans by total spans to calculate the error rate per operation. The result is a ratio between `0` and `1,` where `1` means all operations failed. The query runs as an **instant Prometheus query**, returning a single value for the 10-minute window.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Alerting on span metrics",
        "Detect high error rate"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
