    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0ef32f9c0918784b748c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Sampling](https://grafana.com/docs/tempo/latest/set-up-for-tracing/instrument-send/set-up-collector/tail-sampling/) is a technique used to reduce the amount of collected spans for cost-saving purposes. There are two main strategies which can be combined:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Alerting on span metrics",
        "Consider sampling"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cd408cc1ac4233936b4335774add7a545187fc22",
        "sha256": "7c271591aca8b13f2218029af9a904919669dd7ad0bf2978df084575f3f9c654",
        "lineStart": 289,
        "lineEnd": 289,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md#L289-L289"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.58e098ca9fbe1e412239",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Head sampling**: The decision to record or drop a span is made when the trace begins. The condition can be configured probabilistically (a percentage of traces) or by filtering out certain operations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Alerting on span metrics",
        "Consider sampling"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cd408cc1ac4233936b4335774add7a545187fc22",
        "sha256": "7c271591aca8b13f2218029af9a904919669dd7ad0bf2978df084575f3f9c654",
        "lineStart": 291,
        "lineEnd": 291,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md#L291-L291"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.35fb4064b06e23aeb10f",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Tail sampling**: The decision is made after the trace completes. This allows sampling more interesting operations, such as slow or failing requests.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Alerting on span metrics",
        "Consider sampling"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cd408cc1ac4233936b4335774add7a545187fc22",
        "sha256": "7c271591aca8b13f2218029af9a904919669dd7ad0bf2978df084575f3f9c654",
        "lineStart": 292,
        "lineEnd": 292,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md#L292-L292"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.612175cfd80113b954a6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With **head sampling**, alerting on span metrics should be done with caution, since span metrics will represent only a subset of all traces.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Alerting on span metrics",
        "Consider sampling"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cd408cc1ac4233936b4335774add7a545187fc22",
        "sha256": "7c271591aca8b13f2218029af9a904919669dd7ad0bf2978df084575f3f9c654",
        "lineStart": 294,
        "lineEnd": 294,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md#L294-L294"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1c621ef106b890b5abc7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With **tail sampling**, it’s important to generate span metrics before a sampling decision is made. [Grafana Cloud Adaptive Traces](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana-cloud/adaptive-telemetry/adaptive-traces/) handle this automatically. With Alloy or the OpenTelemetry Collector, make sure the SpanMetrics connector runs before the filtering or [tail sampling processor](https://grafana.com/docs/alloy/latest/reference/components/otelcol/otelcol.processor.tail_sampling/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Alerting on span metrics",
        "Consider sampling"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cd408cc1ac4233936b4335774add7a545187fc22",
        "sha256": "7c271591aca8b13f2218029af9a904919669dd7ad0bf2978df084575f3f9c654",
        "lineStart": 296,
        "lineEnd": 296,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md#L296-L296"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ca181cc9feb48519d823",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "TraceQL is a query language for searching and filtering traces in Grafana Tempo, which uses a syntax similar to `PromQL` and `LogQL`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Using TraceQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cd408cc1ac4233936b4335774add7a545187fc22",
        "sha256": "7c271591aca8b13f2218029af9a904919669dd7ad0bf2978df084575f3f9c654",
        "lineStart": 300,
        "lineEnd": 300,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md#L300-L300"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fb244bbe422472f964d2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With TraceQL, you can skip converting tracing data into span metrics and query raw trace data directly. It provides a more flexible filtering based on the trace structure, attributes, or resource metadata, and can detect issues faster as it doesn't wait for metric generation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Examples of trace-based alerts",
        "Using TraceQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/examples/trace-based-alerts.md",
