    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.59a3e70d18c8159ed068",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Silences](ref:silences) and [mute timings](ref:mute-timings) allow you to pause notifications without interrupting alert rule evaluation. Use a silence to pause notifications on a one-time basis, such as during a maintenance window; and use mute timings to pause notifications at regular intervals, such as evenings and weekends.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Grafana Alerting",
        "Fundamentals",
        "Silences and mute timings"
      ],
