    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a79a7661e37535d22960",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This can occur due to evaluation timeouts (default: `30s`) or repeated failures (default: `3`) when querying the data source. The [`evaluation_timeout`](ref:evaluation_timeout) and [`max_attempts`](ref:max_attempts) options control these settings.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "`Error` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 94,
        "lineEnd": 94,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L94-L94"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.811ee52382da8c575715",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The **Error** state honors the [pending period](ref:pending-period): the alert instance transitions `Normal → Pending → Error`. Set the pending period to `0` to skip the **Pending** state and enter **Error** immediately.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "`Error` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 96,
        "lineEnd": 96,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L96-L96"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c5768d1439aab3901d1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When an alert instance enters the **Error** state, Grafana, by default, triggers a new [`DatasourceError` alert](#no-data-and-error-alerts). You can control this behavior based on the desired outcome of your alert rule in [Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state](#modify-the-no-data-or-error-state).",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "`Error` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
