    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.63f6e2c9e3f62bb90e80",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The **No Data** state occurs when the alert rule query runs successfully but returns no data points at all.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "`No Data` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 102,
        "lineEnd": 102,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L102-L102"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f8b5505628869ee65f07",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The **No Data** state honors the [pending period](ref:pending-period): the alert instance transitions `Normal → Pending → No Data`. Set the pending period to `0` to skip the **Pending** state and enter **No Data** immediately.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "`No Data` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 104,
        "lineEnd": 104,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L104-L104"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.87294e49dceb372b07e0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When an alert instance enters the **No Data** state, Grafana, by default, triggers a new [`DatasourceNoData` alert](#no-data-and-error-alerts). You can control this behavior based on the desired outcome of your alert rule in [Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state](#modify-the-no-data-or-error-state).",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "`No Data` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 106,
        "lineEnd": 106,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L106-L106"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a169c467c5770fc2c466",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In [Configure no data and error handling](ref:no-data-and-error-handling), you can configure the behavior when the evaluation returns no data or all values are null:",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 112,
        "lineEnd": 112,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L112-L112"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cb1b18dfcfe491e175ff",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also configure the behavior when the evaluation returns an error or timeout:",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 116,
        "lineEnd": 116,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L116-L116"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1f9c0145ee4534babdbe",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Note that when you configure the **No Data** or **Error** behavior to set the **Alerting** or **Normal** state, Grafana attempts to keep a stable set of fields under notification `Values`. If your query returns no data or an error, Grafana re-uses the latest known set of fields in `Values`, but will use `-1` in place of the measured value.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 120,
        "lineEnd": 120,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L120-L120"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.db18a0a7dee8f1f9ed3b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When an alert rule evaluation results in a `No Data` or `Error` state, Grafana Alerting creates a new alert instance with the following additional labels:",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state",
        "`No Data` and `Error` alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
