    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7f09d65b869b555326da",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can manage these alerts like regular ones by using their labels to apply actions such as adding a silence, routing via notification policies, and more.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state",
        "`No Data` and `Error` alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 138,
        "lineEnd": 138,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L138-L138"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.102f64afada7cd5d5e64",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If the alert rule is configured to send notifications directly to a selected contact point (instead of using notification policies), the `DatasourceNoData` and `DatasourceError` alerts are also sent to that contact point. Any additional notification settings defined in the alert rule, such as muting or grouping, are preserved.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state",
        "`No Data` and `Error` alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 140,
        "lineEnd": 140,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L140-L140"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.32127d4b395438d075f0",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. Use the **Keep last state** option. For more information, refer to the section below. This option allows the alert to retain its last known state when there is no data available, rather than switching to a **No Data** state.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state",
        "Reduce `No Data` or `Error` alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 146,
        "lineEnd": 146,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L146-L146"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d55fd489a9486de2adc7",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. For **No Data** alerts, you can optimize your alert rule by expanding the time range of the query. However, if the time range is too big, it affects the performance of the query and can lead to errors due to timeout.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state",
        "Reduce `No Data` or `Error` alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 147,
        "lineEnd": 147,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L147-L147"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6a39f41e69cdeb9ddba9",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. Consider increasing the [pending period](ref:pending-period). Since the **No Data** and **Error** states honor the pending period, a longer period can suppress `DatasourceNoData` and `DatasourceError` notifications for transient issues.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state",
        "Reduce `No Data` or `Error` alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 151,
        "lineEnd": 151,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L151-L151"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4ae88146b5533ebea68e",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. To reduce multiple notifications from **Error** alerts, define a [notification policy](ref:notification-policies) to handle all related alerts with `alertname=DatasourceError`, and filter and group errors from the same data source using the `datasource_uid` label.",
      "headingPath": [
        "No Data and Error states",
        "Modify the `No Data` or `Error` state",
        "Reduce `No Data` or `Error` alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f2f978a5edf34654e0b6cfc6238773eb52ed2854",
        "sha256": "b2ee34090eb03b41b5a98cc5e30a4f89026d2d107741ed9b6c5d1018e0b81df2",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 153,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states.md#L153-L153"
