    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.48bf74ba5b0756a165c2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Labels** are unique identifiers of an [alert instance](ref:alert-instances). You can use them for searching, silencing, and routing notifications.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Labels and annotations",
        "Labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/annotation-label.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "27ae61e3cb9b8c453a56fde68e7b11bc84734fc5",
        "sha256": "f11b0b24845d9463ffc2a12709008f455d230982ef999ef627c075d475ac226d",
        "lineStart": 67,
        "lineEnd": 67,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/annotation-label.md#L67-L67"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9bb46dcd0fd253cba024",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Examples of labels are `server=server1` or `team=backend`. Each alert rule can have more than one label and the complete set of labels for an alert rule is called its label set. It is this label set that identifies the alert.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Labels and annotations",
        "Labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/annotation-label.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "27ae61e3cb9b8c453a56fde68e7b11bc84734fc5",
        "sha256": "f11b0b24845d9463ffc2a12709008f455d230982ef999ef627c075d475ac226d",
        "lineStart": 69,
        "lineEnd": 69,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/annotation-label.md#L69-L69"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.be11f587db12a8502f52",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, an alert instance might have the label set `{alertname=\"High CPU usage\",server=\"server1\"}` while another alert instance might have the label set `{alertname=\"High CPU usage\",server=\"server2\"}`. These are two separate alert instances because although their `alertname` labels are the same, their `server` labels are different.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Labels and annotations",
        "Labels"
      ],
