    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3441daf2731092e41bd1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerting periodically runs the queries and expressions, evaluating the condition. If the condition is breached, an alert instance is triggered for each time series.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Queries and conditions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/queries-conditions.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "552ed8aeffdfa414ba93a5e202cd372a2c5004fa",
        "sha256": "5a45c7a1167e0656a3c24f733bc9219d36fcf33f18bd1e16bd1a04eb4fa85296",
        "lineStart": 77,
        "lineEnd": 77,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/queries-conditions.md#L77-L77"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.410754e8e8db4b2ebab9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Queries in Grafana can be applied in various ways, depending on the data source and query language being used. Each data source’s query editor provides a customized user interface to help you write queries that take advantage of its unique capabilities. For details about query editors and syntax in Grafana, refer to [Query and transform data](ref:query-transform-data).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Queries and conditions",
        "Data source queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/queries-conditions.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "552ed8aeffdfa414ba93a5e202cd372a2c5004fa",
        "sha256": "5a45c7a1167e0656a3c24f733bc9219d36fcf33f18bd1e16bd1a04eb4fa85296",
        "lineStart": 83,
        "lineEnd": 83,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/queries-conditions.md#L83-L83"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2099ce9e985cffc3786b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerting can work with two types of data:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Queries and conditions",
        "Data source queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/queries-conditions.md",
