    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.27d3106808fdc8515dc7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can explore [this alert example in Grafana Play](https://play.grafana.org/alerting/grafana/qp_db_utilization_forecast/view?tab=query&tech=docs&pg=alerting-examples&plcmt=callout-tip&cta=db-utilization-forecast-alert-example).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert on a future prediction"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 155,
        "lineEnd": 155,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L155-L155"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert on a future prediction"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bb78e49359f5c7b26bcb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A forecast-based alert can also detect when the current signal deviates from the prediction.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 160,
        "lineEnd": 160,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L160-L160"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7d22f7ec1f733865b69c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the previous examples, forecast alerts detect potential future situations: they alert when a signal is expected to exceed a threshold at some point in the future. The key differences in this case are:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 162,
        "lineEnd": 162,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L162-L162"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.81fb0ecfc2309ea20653",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. The alert does not look for a future threshold breach. Instead, it compares the current value with the forecast range and alerts when the actual value falls outside the forecast range.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 164,
        "lineEnd": 164,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L164-L164"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.66a204cc0678f4fd0eb3",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "2. The forecast acts as an **adaptive baseline**. While a standard alert rule evaluates the signal against a fixed threshold, a forecast-based alert rule evaluates the signal against the forecast, which can change over time based on seasonal patterns.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 165,
        "lineEnd": 165,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L165-L165"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8feb47a90d45c242653f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For alerting, each forecast produces an [anomalous metric](/docs/grafana-cloud/ai-tools/machine-learning/forecasting/detect-anomalies/#the-anomalous-metric) (`<forecast_metric_name>:anomalous`) that returns `0` when the actual value is within the prediction interval. You can use this metric directly in a forecast alert:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 169,
        "lineEnd": 169,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L169-L169"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d2fcbcaea3e9d880beb0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also configure an alert to fire only when the actual value exceeds the predicted upper bound.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast",
        "Alert only on unexpectedly high values"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 178,
        "lineEnd": 178,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L178-L178"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast > Alert only on unexpectedly high values"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.df987dc880305e013255",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this case, the alert rule can also query `<forecast_metric_name>:anomalous`, which returns `1` when the actual value is above the upper bound and `-1` when it is below the lower bound:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast",
        "Alert only on unexpectedly high values"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a541d1b6c0359fd96613a0e62af6b19ece7ffcc8",
        "sha256": "40f628b968dfea7505d678fab42d587cb94c26022292423de09a2034dbad018c",
        "lineStart": 182,
        "lineEnd": 182,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/alerting-on-forecasts.md#L182-L182"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Alerting on forecasts > Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning > Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast > Alert only on unexpectedly high values"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.97ef21b4b7eea8f0057e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alternatively, you can compare the actual value directly with the predicted upper bound:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting on forecasts",
        "Seasonal forecast with Grafana Cloud Machine Learning",
        "Alert when the actual state is outside the forecast",
        "Alert only on unexpectedly high values"
      ],
      "source": {
