        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.30ae9663f94229ace020",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerts should primarily detect user-facing failures, not internal component behavior. Users don't care that a pod restarted; they care when the application is slow or failing. Symptom-based alerts tie directly to user impact.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prioritize symptoms, but don’t ignore infrastructure signals"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 88,
        "lineEnd": 88,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L88-L88"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.710ea1652e83ec2babca",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "That said, infrastructure signals still matter. They can act as early warning indicators and are often useful when alerting maturity is low. A sustained spike in CPU or memory usage might not justify a page, but it can help explain or anticipate symptom-based failures.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prioritize symptoms, but don’t ignore infrastructure signals"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 92,
        "lineEnd": 92,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L92-L92"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.45fea5d7a87d9d44a78b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Infrastructure alerts tend to be noisy and are often ignored when treated like paging signals. They are usually better suited for lower-severity channels such as dashboards, alert lists, or non-paging destinations like a dedicated Slack channel, where they can be monitored without interrupting on-call.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prioritize symptoms, but don’t ignore infrastructure signals"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 94,
        "lineEnd": 94,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L94-L94"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.98474a25032447e90398",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The key is balance as your alerting matures. Use infrastructure alerts to support diagnosis and prevention, not as a replacement for symptom-based alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prioritize symptoms, but don’t ignore infrastructure signals"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 96,
        "lineEnd": 96,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L96-L96"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.114b40fc04abb8620690",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alert priority is often tied to user impact and the urgency to respond, but confidence should determine when escalation is necessary.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Escalate priority based on confidence"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 100,
        "lineEnd": 100,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L100-L100"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.25ebc283f38f73d58428",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this context, escalation defines how responders are notified as confidence grows. This can include increasing alert priority, widening notification, paging additional responders, or opening an incident once intervention is clearly required.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Escalate priority based on confidence"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 102,
        "lineEnd": 102,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L102-L102"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.463c9f2c732a4d2da295",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Early signals are often ambiguous, and confidence in a non-transient failure is usually low. Paging too early creates noise; paging too late means users are impacted for longer before anyone acts. A small or sudden increase in latency may not justify immediate action, but it can indicate a failure in progress.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Escalate priority based on confidence"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 104,
        "lineEnd": 104,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L104-L104"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bb218ae3fbab7db2ca32",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Escalation is justified when issues are sustained or reinforced by multiple signals. For example, high latency combined with a rising error rate, or the same event firing over a sustained period. These patterns reduce the chance of transient noise and increase the likelihood of real impact.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Escalate priority based on confidence"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 108,
        "lineEnd": 108,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L108-L108"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.65be864f9f3573d3650a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use confidence in user impact to drive escalation and avoid unnecessary pages.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Escalate priority based on confidence"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 110,
        "lineEnd": 110,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L110-L110"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bd06beab25ed113b1054",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In distributed systems, avoid creating separate alert rules for every host, service, or endpoint. Instead, define alert rules that scale automatically using [multi-dimensional alert rules](ref:multi-dimensional-alerts). This reduces rule duplication and allows alerting to scale as the system grows.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Scope alerts for scalability and actionability"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 114,
        "lineEnd": 114,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L114-L114"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.841b3d4b7e9f1923f73a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Start simple. Default to a single dimension such as `service` or `endpoint` to keep alerts manageable. Add dimensions only when they improve actionability. For example, when missing a dimension like `region` hides failures or doesn't provide enough information to act quickly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Scope alerts for scalability and actionability"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 116,
        "lineEnd": 116,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L116-L116"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.80094c22648cb28a2b86",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Additional dimensions like `region` or `instance` can help identify the root cause, but more isn't always better.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Scope alerts for scalability and actionability"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 118,
        "lineEnd": 118,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L118-L118"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0b746132acfc2ae30e8a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerts should be designed for the first responder, not the person who created the alert. Anyone on call should be able to understand what's wrong and what to do next without deep knowledge of the system or alert configuration.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Design alerts for first responders and clear actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 122,
        "lineEnd": 122,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L122-L122"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.54a9e5d5f4e56bdde773",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Avoid vague alerts that force responders to spend time figuring out context. Every alert should clearly explain why it exists, what triggered it, and how to investigate. Use [annotations](ref:annotations) to link to relevant dashboards and runbooks, which are essential for faster resolution.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Design alerts for first responders and clear actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 124,
        "lineEnd": 124,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L124-L124"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a3f3a6e50ce86b155911",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerts should indicate a real problem and be actionable, even if the impact is low. Informational alerts add noise without improving reliability.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Design alerts for first responders and clear actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 126,
        "lineEnd": 126,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L126-L126"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.54a59adb42deaa91a3f5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If no action is possible, it shouldn't be an alert—consider using a dashboard instead. Over time, alerts behave like technical debt: easy to create, costly to maintain, and hard to remove.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Design alerts for first responders and clear actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 128,
        "lineEnd": 128,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L128-L128"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.479e6d66cb6cfc3bc558",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Review alerts often and remove those that don’t lead to action.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Design alerts for first responders and clear actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 130,
        "lineEnd": 130,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L130-L130"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c6c152977f26ed78898d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerts without ownership are often ignored. Every alert must have an owner: a team responsible for maintaining the alert and responding when it fires.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Alerts should have an owner and system scope"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 134,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L134-L134"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fbe485ded4685e0fc849",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerts must also define a system scope, such as a service or infrastructure component. Scope provides organizational context and connects alerts with ownership. Defining clear scopes is easier when services are treated as first-class entities, and organizations are built around service ownership.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Alerts should have an owner and system scope"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.41943893ac6353b6d09a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "> [Service Center in Grafana Cloud](/docs/grafana-cloud/alerting-and-irm/service-center/) can help operate a service-oriented view of your system and align alert scope with ownership.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Alerts should have an owner and system scope"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 138,
        "lineEnd": 138,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L138-L138"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.22f1f455c3441af9461a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerts should be delivered to the right team and channel based on priority, ownership, and team workflows. Use [notification policies](ref:notification-policies) to define a routing tree that matches the context of your service or scope:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Alerts should have an owner and system scope"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 142,
        "lineEnd": 142,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L142-L142"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.02b3037579406928c96f",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Define a parent policy for default routing within the scope.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Alerts should have an owner and system scope"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
