      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9411e4f621fb13ed6c0a",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Define nested policies for specific cases or higher-priority issues.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Alerts should have an owner and system scope"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 145,
        "lineEnd": 145,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L145-L145"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ff7eab5136e215bd303d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Without alert grouping, responders can receive many notifications for the same underlying problem.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prevent notification overload with alert grouping"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 149,
        "lineEnd": 149,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L149-L149"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.71f641166372714d4b4f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, a database failure can trigger several alerts at the same time like increased latency, higher error rates, and internal errors. Paging separately for each symptom quickly turns into notification spam, even though there is a single root cause.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prevent notification overload with alert grouping"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 151,
        "lineEnd": 151,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L151-L151"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.231b57b185bfaf1d9169",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Notification grouping](ref:group-alert-notifications) consolidates related alerts into a single notification. Instead of receiving multiple pages for the same issue, responders get one alert that represents the incident and includes all related firing alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prevent notification overload with alert grouping"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 153,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L153-L153"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b767de269b053eccef64",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grouping should follow operational boundaries such as service or owner, as defined by notification policies. Downstream or cascading failures should be grouped together so they surface as one issue rather than many.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prevent notification overload with alert grouping"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 155,
        "lineEnd": 155,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L155-L155"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.05b13706491d64658d59",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "There is also a limit to how many notifications can be sent out per second. You can configure your Contact Point settings to reduce the email expenditure by setting up single email notifications rather than individual email notifications. To configure this, go to your desired email Contact Point and enable **Single email** in the [optional settings](ref:email-optional-settings).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Prevent notification overload with alert grouping"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 157,
        "lineEnd": 157,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L157-L157"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c7655b70e22d43009545",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Require issues to persist before alerting. Set a [pending period](ref:pending-period) to define how long a condition must remain true before firing. For example, instead of alerting immediately on high error rate, require it to stay above the threshold for some minutes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Mitigate flapping alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 163,
        "lineEnd": 163,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L163-L163"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.788168ca6aa1a50a68f5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Also, stabilize alerts by tuning query ranges and aggregations. Using raw data makes alerts sensitive to noise. Instead, evaluate over a time window and aggregate the data to smooth short spikes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Mitigate flapping alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 165,
        "lineEnd": 165,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L165-L165"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4af88aaadf06b9f12170",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When a symptom-based alert fires frequently, it usually indicates a reliability concern that should be measured and managed more deliberately. This is often a sign that the alert could evolve into an [service level objective (SLO)](/docs/grafana-cloud/alerting-and-irm/slo/introduction).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Graduate symptom-based alerts into SLOs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 185,
        "lineEnd": 185,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L185-L185"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e19d20a2307a1e219029",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Traditional alerts create pressure to react immediately, while error budgets introduce a buffer of time to act, changing how urgency is handled. Alerts can then be defined in terms of error budget burn rate rather than reacting to every minor deviation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Graduate symptom-based alerts into SLOs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 187,
        "lineEnd": 187,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L187-L187"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e8de825d654665167aa1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, instead of several teams alerting on high latency, a single SLO can be used across teams to capture overall API performance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Graduate symptom-based alerts into SLOs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 191,
        "lineEnd": 191,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L191-L191"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3a5848364248a8924cec",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For other use cases, refer to [when alerts need an SLO](ref:when-slos-reduce-alert-noise).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Graduate symptom-based alerts into SLOs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 193,
        "lineEnd": 193,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L193-L193"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fb86a1aacc21cbf77c8b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use [silences](ref:silences) during active incidents to reduce repeated notifications, but scope them carefully to avoid silencing unrelated alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Integrate alerting into incident post-mortems"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 201,
        "lineEnd": 201,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L201-L201"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f207d155c6345494036f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Post-mortems should evaluate alerts with root causes and lessons learned. If responders lacked key information during the incident, enrich alerts with additional context, dashboards, or better guidance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Alerting best practices",
        "Integrate alerting into incident post-mortems"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "618b4722456e2e8bfa8d9a19e832ace6411c8977",
        "sha256": "311c2ba48756f7de84fb05e428c1ced7512246429640a2ed7de9ff9672b4df49",
        "lineStart": 203,
        "lineEnd": 203,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/best-practices.md#L203-L203"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
