    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3d62e8145ff0ed75041e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this example, waiting for 5 minutes means the single scrape error won't result in a fired alert. Since Prometheus scrapes metrics every minute by default, the alert only fires after five consecutive failures.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
