    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1fbd670ad576910ec051",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A single recovery resets the alert, that’s why `up == 0 for: 5m` can sometimes be unreliable. Even if the target is down most of the time, the alert didn't fire, leaving you unaware of a potential persistent issue.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
