        "lineStart": 125,
        "lineEnd": 125,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L125-L125"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.11508162264922ecd84b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This alert rule fires when the target is unreachable for more than 20% of the last 10 minutes, rather than looking for consecutive scrape failures. With a one minute scrape interval, three or more failed scrapes within the last 10 minutes now triggers the alert.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric",
        "Use `avg_over_time` to smooth signal"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 133,
        "lineEnd": 133,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L133-L133"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6e5251b3520ac46c7000",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Since this query uses a threshold and time window to control accuracy, you can now lower the `for` duration (or [pending period](ref:pending-period) in Grafana) to something shorter—`0m` or `1m`—so the alert fires faster.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric",
        "Use `avg_over_time` to smooth signal"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
