    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.744cb28d5a90286fe0c8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Blackbox Exporter exposes the results of these checks as metrics, which Prometheus can scrape like any other target. For example, the `probe_success` metric reports whether the probe was able to reach the service. The setup looks like this:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric",
        "Use synthetic checks to monitor external availability"
      ],
