      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3454a9021f1fd87bf650",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To detect when a service isn’t reachable externally, you can define an alert using the `probe_success` metric:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric",
        "Use synthetic checks to monitor external availability"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 151,
        "lineEnd": 151,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L151-L151"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4faa329ebf2340a70c53",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This alert fires when the probe has failed continuously for 5 minutes—indicating that the service couldn’t be reached from the outside.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric",
        "Use synthetic checks to monitor external availability"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 155,
        "lineEnd": 155,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L155-L155"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.09c60def0ff4d68cb864",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can then combine internal and external checks to make the detection of connectivity errors more reliable. This alert catches when the internal scrape fails or the service is externally unreachable.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric",
        "Use synthetic checks to monitor external availability"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 157,
        "lineEnd": 157,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L157-L157"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6e72b725cec3e66405a2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This alert fires when Prometheus couldn't scrape the target successfully for more than 20% of the past 10 minutes, or when the external probes have been failing more than 20% of the time. This smoothing technique can be applied to any binary availability signal.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Detect target availability with the Prometheus `up` metric",
        "Use synthetic checks to monitor external availability"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 165,
        "lineEnd": 165,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L165-L165"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.773443a375003cc58ed7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If your alert only checks the general `up` metric without breaking it down by labels (like `instance`, `host`, or `pod`), you might miss when a host stops reporting. For example, an alert that looks only at the aggregated status of all instances will likely fail to catch when individual instances go missing.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Manage offline hosts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 171,
        "lineEnd": 171,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L171-L171"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ecf78aee857cb2391652",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This isn't a connectivity error in this context — it’s not that the alert or Prometheus can't reach anything, it’s that one or more specific targets have gone silent. These kinds of problems aren’t caught by `up == 0` alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Manage offline hosts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 173,
        "lineEnd": 173,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L173-L173"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5f63aab1fe6f47f8c7a9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For these cases, see the complementary [guide on handling missing data](ref:missing-data-guide) — it covers common scenarios where the alert queries return no data at all, or where only some targets stop reporting. These aren't full availability failures or execution errors, but they can still lead to blind spots in alert detection.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Manage offline hosts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 175,
        "lineEnd": 175,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L175-L175"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f4e9ce8b7b1efbd2c4ca",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Not all connectivity issues come from targets going offline. Sometimes, the alert rule fails when querying its target. These aren’t availability problems—they’re query execution errors: maybe the data source timed out, the network dropped, or the query was invalid.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 179,
        "lineEnd": 179,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L179-L179"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.952b95308d69b2302795",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This difference matters. Availability issues are typically handled using metrics like `up` or `probe_success` but execution errors require a different setup.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 183,
        "lineEnd": 183,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L183-L183"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f89c0d68075ca60d7610",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Alerting has built-in handling for execution errors, regardless of the data source. That includes Prometheus, and others like Graphite, InfluxDB, PostgreSQL, etc. By default, Grafana Alerting automatically handles query errors so you don’t miss critical failures. When an alert rule fails to execute, Grafana fires a special `DatasourceError` alert.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 185,
        "lineEnd": 185,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L185-L185"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e99f2fff96a24b340d21",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can configure this behavior depending on how critical the alert is and on whether you already have other alerts detecting the issue. In [**Configure no data and error handling**](ref:configure-nodata-and-error-handling), click **Alert state if execution error or timeout**, and choose the desired option for the alert:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 187,
        "lineEnd": 187,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L187-L187"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.158e2e598cc786e37421",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Error (default)**: Triggers a separate `DatasourceError` alert. This default ensures alert rules always inform about query errors but can create noise.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 189,
        "lineEnd": 189,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L189-L189"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.186cdce40204fa2c32c1",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Alerting**: Treats the error as if the alert condition is firing. Grafana transitions all existing instances for that rule to the `Alerting` state.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 190,
        "lineEnd": 190,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L190-L190"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fba8698de47197ee8acc",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Normal**: Ignores the query error and transitions all alert instances to the `Normal` state. This is useful if the error isn’t critical or if you already have other alerts detecting connectivity issues.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 191,
        "lineEnd": 191,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L191-L191"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.81944dee2fb6e16a8e20",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Keep Last State**: Keeps the previous state until the query succeeds again. Suitable for unstable environments to avoid flapping alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 192,
        "lineEnd": 192,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L192-L192"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.df43fec8ba5e88abd2b6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This applies even when alert rules query Prometheus itself—not just external data sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 196,
        "lineEnd": 196,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L196-L196"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.20ccca72eda4e1080b6d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In practice, start by deciding if you want to create explicit alert rules — for example, using `up` or `probe_success` — to detect when a target is down or has connectivity issues.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting",
        "Design alerts for connectivity errors"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 200,
        "lineEnd": 200,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L200-L200"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9b5dc843689c2739c943",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A single data source error can lead to multiple alerts firing simultaneously, sometimes bombarding you with many alerts and generating too much noise.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting",
        "Reduce redundant error notifications"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
