    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.48c6961f24cb12f3dc4e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As described previously, you can control the error-handling behavior for Grafana alerts. The **Keep Last State** or **Normal** option prevents alerts from firing and helps avoid redundant alerts, especially for services already covered by `up` or `probe_success` alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Handle query errors in Grafana Alerting",
        "Reduce redundant error notifications"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
