    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c59633b0aff1507fc9c2",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Availability issues**, where the target itself is down or unreachable (e.g., due to a crash or network failure).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 224,
        "lineEnd": 224,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L224-L224"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b21cce55c4ae9c742095",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Query execution errors**, where the alert rule can't reach its data source (e.g., due to timeouts, invalid queries, or data source outages).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 226,
        "lineEnd": 226,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L226-L226"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d706ef7e907321ed28a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "These problems come from different parts of your stack, and require its own techniques. Prometheus and Grafana allow you to detect them, and combining distinct techniques can make your alerts more resilient.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 228,
        "lineEnd": 228,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L228-L228"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8b911b3cfda7225fd295",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Prometheus, avoid relying solely on `up == 0`. Smooth queries to account for intermittent failures, and use synthetic monitoring to detect reachability issues from outside your network.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 230,
        "lineEnd": 230,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L230-L230"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4e87577280a547037ce1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana Alerting, configure error handling explicitly. Not all alerts are equal or have the same urgency. Tune the error-handling behavior based on the reliability and severity of the alerts and whether you already have alerts dedicated to connectivity problems.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 232,
        "lineEnd": 232,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L232-L232"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f4769fd337d7dd8793d1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "And don’t forget the third case: **missing data**. If only one host from a fleet silently disappears, you might not get alerted. If you're dealing with individual instances that stopped reporting data, see the [Guide on handling missing data](ref:missing-data-guide) to continue exploring this topic.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle connectivity errors in alerts",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ac013ad7e78eb6f989a82991e5d246600a3e436d",
        "sha256": "a3943a943a9907ac7c1b3b13ba6b8f1519bbda6b9a19cf01591f2ade20d35b63",
        "lineStart": 234,
        "lineEnd": 234,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/connectivity-errors.md#L234-L234"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72a35c733e3fe3c37d8d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Missing data from when a target stops reporting metric data can be one of the most common issues when troubleshooting alerts. In cloud-native environments, this happens all the time. Pods or nodes scale down to match demand, or an entire job quietly disappears.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f6987c75ef55eaa82a89",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When this happens, alerts won’t fire, and you might not notice the system has stopped reporting.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 62,
        "lineEnd": 62,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L62-L62"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bdf85d22514666976988",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This guide covers different scenarios where the underlying data is missing and shows how to design your alerts to act on those cases. If you're troubleshooting an unreachable host or a network failure, see the [Handle connectivity errors documentation](ref:connectivity-errors-guide) as well.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
