    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c10da984c69ed295aed6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alert queries often return multiple time series — one per instance, pod, region, or label combination. This is known as a **multi-dimensional alert**, meaning a single alert rule can trigger multiple alert instances (alerts).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "No Data vs. Missing Series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
