      "id": "grafana.candidate.ffb841a8098e965869d3",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| 02:00 | 1.4s 🟢 | 1s 🟢             | ✅ No Alert                  |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "No Data vs. Missing Series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 106,
        "lineEnd": 106,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L106-L106"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0be3daa862fec6ca0be2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Prometheus doesn't fire alerts when the query returns no data. It simply assumes there was nothing to report, like with query errors. Missing data won’t trigger existing alerts unless you explicitly check for it.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Detect missing data in Prometheus"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 112,
        "lineEnd": 112,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L112-L112"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9e8d02c107cb476b0fe9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Prometheus, a common way to catch missing data is by to use the `absent_over_time` function.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Detect missing data in Prometheus"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 114,
        "lineEnd": 114,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L114-L114"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.887b03b2d3a1e08fe314",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This triggers when all series for `http_request_latency_seconds` are absent for 5 minutes — catching the _No Data_ case when the entire metric disappears.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Detect missing data in Prometheus"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 118,
        "lineEnd": 118,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L118-L118"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.775bafa743f6c277fa59",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "However, `absent_over_time()` can’t detect which specific series are missing since it doesn’t preserve labels. The alert won’t tell you which series stopped reporting, only that the query returns no data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Detect missing data in Prometheus"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 120,
        "lineEnd": 120,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L120-L120"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.89ae80f030e1af29787a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you want to check for missing data per-region or label, you can specify the label in the alert query as follows:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Detect missing data in Prometheus"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 122,
        "lineEnd": 122,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L122-L122"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.df76ba0a20982808daa7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "But this doesn't scale well. It is unreliable to have hard-coded queries for each label set, especially in dynamic cloud environments where instances can appear or disappear at any time.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Detect missing data in Prometheus"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 132,
        "lineEnd": 132,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L132-L132"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.361fa9201f44b3dfab15",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To detect when a specific target has disappeared, see below **Evict alert instances for missing series** for details on how Grafana handles this case and how to set up detection.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Detect missing data in Prometheus"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 134,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L134-L134"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.081f9ca5d38f1b19eb23",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "While Prometheus provides functions like `absent_over_time()` to detect missing data, not all data sources — like Graphite, InfluxDB, PostgreSQL, and others — available to Grafana alerts support a similar function.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 138,
        "lineEnd": 138,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L138-L138"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3d3e96647d49bd7bc15e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To handle this, Grafana Alerting implements a built-in `No Data` state logic, so you don’t need to detect missing data with `absent_*` queries. Instead, you can configure in the alert rule settings how alerts behave when no data is returned.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 140,
        "lineEnd": 140,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L140-L140"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.601f9a1fd84db41653fb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Similar to error handling, Grafana triggers a special _No data_ alert by default and lets you control this behavior. In [**Configure no data and error handling**](ref:configure-nodata-and-error-handling), click **Alert state if no data or all values are null**, and choose one of the following options:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 142,
        "lineEnd": 142,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L142-L142"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.41e56c0f84d9a75b96c1",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **No Data (default):** Triggers a new `DatasourceNoData` alert, treating _No data_ as a specific problem.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 144,
        "lineEnd": 144,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L144-L144"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3e42847068a81cead19b",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Alerting:** Transition each existing alert instance into the `Alerting` state when data disappears.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 145,
        "lineEnd": 145,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L145-L145"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.64459aabdf4dee3c04a9",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Normal:** Ignores missing data and transitions all instances to the `Normal` state. Useful when receiving intermittent data, such as from experimental services, sporadic actions, or periodic reports.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 146,
        "lineEnd": 146,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L146-L146"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.498c34e9cbd6823c6bc0",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Keep Last State:** Leaves the alert in its previous state until the data returns. This is common in environments where brief metric gaps happen regularly, like with flaky exporters or noisy environments.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 147,
        "lineEnd": 147,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L147-L147"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8ce8d4281f8809c0aa45",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When Grafana triggers a [NoData alert](ref:no-data-and-error-alerts), it creates a distinct alert instance, separate from the original alert instance. These alerts behave differently:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
        "Manage No Data issues in Grafana alerts",
        "Manage DatasourceNoData notifications"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8816ddb5943b9f021d5f7758a11dafd170578791",
        "sha256": "bde64b9c1372e92555c153fdb5fbad273ee00be9c7ff4b8ae0113e22ce54dc2b",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 153,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/missing-data.md#L153-L153"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f8b5f33a08160ded7a73",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- They use a dedicated `alertname: DatasourceNoData`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Handle missing data in Grafana Alerting",
