    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a4df1be3fb656cf784ea",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As your alerting setup grows in production, not every alert works as expected. Sometimes they fire too often, or they resolve immediately before anyone responds. You start wondering if the problem is the alert.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 34,
        "lineEnd": 34,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L34-L34"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9bf644ebcc9c04094e0d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When this happens, your instinct may be to tune the query or threshold, or maybe just delete it. Sometimes the alert is telling you that you're measuring reliability wrong, and implementing [service level objectives (SLOs)](/docs/grafana-cloud/alerting-and-irm/slo/introduction/) could be the right answer.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 36,
        "lineEnd": 36,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L36-L36"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4547f709868362930ed0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This guide covers the three most common patterns where SLOs can help reduce alert noise and improve reliability coverage, and shows how to recognize the need for SLOs in your alerting setup.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 38,
        "lineEnd": 38,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L38-L38"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.65269c52003a02635551",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If the query result crosses the threshold at that moment, the alert fires. It continues in a firing state on the next evaluation if the condition still holds, or returns to normal once resolved.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 44,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L44-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cdb109b5e519cec59f1e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- An alert asks: over the past 10 minutes, did 50% of requests respond in under 3s?",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 52,
        "lineEnd": 52,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L52-L52"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.30a92cf6c4ddff1d8e0e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- An SLO asks a similar question over a longer window: over the past 4 weeks, did 95% of requests respond in under 3 seconds?",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 54,
        "lineEnd": 54,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L54-L54"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7e9d48a29e9babd747ea",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerts can also use long evaluation periods, but they reset when the service recovers.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 56,
        "lineEnd": 56,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L56-L56"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c6a936cfe7d6aaebce68",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "SLOs track failures against the [error budget](/grafana-cloud/alerting-and-irm/slo/introduction/#error-budget) even when the service recovers. They record how much degradation has accumulated, and report how much failure is still allowed.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 58,
        "lineEnd": 58,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L58-L58"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6d5ec9ae1635e06f4efd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Another key difference is how [SLO alerts](/grafana-cloud/alerting-and-irm/slo/set-up/configure-burn-rate-notifications/#burn-rate-alert-rule-conditions) work. Rather than firing when the error budget is consumed and the objective is breached, they **fire when the objective is at risk**.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 62,
        "lineEnd": 62,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L62-L62"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.61ac169ab2d43f466ea7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "SLO alerts page you when the system is degrading quickly, so you have time to act before breaching the SLO.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 64,
        "lineEnd": 64,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L64-L64"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4e44f0c3de7b02776aaa",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "SLOs and threshold-based alerts are complementary. In some cases, tracking the same reliability signal in both alerts and SLOs makes sense: alerts for immediate response and SLOs for long-term visibility. In others, graduating alerts to SLOs is the right call. The following cases are the most common situations where teams start adopting SLOs from existing alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "How SLOs differ from threshold alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 66,
        "lineEnd": 66,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L66-L66"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bc84789f34289b130558",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Alerts should be actionable](ref:design-alerts-for-first-responders-and-clear-actions). An alert nobody acts on is operational noise. If the alert consistently triggers no response, but the metric still matters to your team, this is a reliability concern.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert has no actionable response"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 70,
        "lineEnd": 70,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L70-L70"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.44a54524d584c38043b5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Ask the team: will we commit to an objective on the health of this service and act if performance degrades? If the answer is yes, an SLO is the right fit.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert has no actionable response"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 74,
        "lineEnd": 74,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L74-L74"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1b95b452ed595d0b08a7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Defining the SLO objective aligns the team around a shared target and determines when accumulated degradation is severe enough to require action. This is frequently the hardest part. Expect a few iterations before the objective reflects reality.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert has no actionable response"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 80,
        "lineEnd": 80,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L80-L80"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c56b1d2b3e870920af61",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Sometimes deleting the alert is the right call if there's no commitment or SLI to anchor to a valid SLO. But if the same metric keeps surfacing in post-mortems across teams, that's a different signal that points to a shared reliability concern.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert has no actionable response"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 82,
        "lineEnd": 82,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L82-L82"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.87158fcb47fcbcb10a3d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When distinct teams define their own thresholds for service performance or user-experience metrics, this reveals a shared user-experience concern that hasn't been made explicit.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert reflects a shared reliability concern"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 90,
        "lineEnd": 90,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L90-L90"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f21d78d358d4586dc6aa",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Creating a shared SLO should not eliminate existing related alerts. This is a good moment to evaluate whether existing alerts trigger immediate action. If you notice these alerts are less actionable, and that the underlying reliability metric is better measured as an SLO, then migrate the existing alert to a team-scoped SLO.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert reflects a shared reliability concern"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 98,
        "lineEnd": 98,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L98-L98"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.038e7048ddbde65306f0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A team-scoped SLO is the safer default. Move to a shared SLO only once teams agree on ownership.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert reflects a shared reliability concern"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 100,
        "lineEnd": 100,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L100-L100"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2f0c23022d8e09abdc4d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alerting best practices recommend [tuning away flapping alerts](ref:mitigate-flapping-alerts) by tweaking alert rule settings to avoid detecting short spikes and transient issues. Tuning reduces noise, but can remove the signal entirely.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert fires on transient conditions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 108,
        "lineEnd": 108,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L108-L108"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ab7bef9065c7e8d3ef00",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this case, the flapping alert has surfaced a reliability issue. Individual firings look harmless, but the accumulated degradation over time impacts users. **A threshold-based alert can mask these errors**.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert fires on transient conditions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 112,
        "lineEnd": 112,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L112-L112"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7cd92df5c0bec6380459",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Tracking reliability signals in dashboards and alerting on long evaluation periods can be the solution. SLOs are the better fit: the error budget doesn't reset and tracks every failure within the SLO window.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "The alert fires on transient conditions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "230351cfa7c2f3948e284f5efb1ce44c475c3a02",
        "sha256": "2ba478102159facc05a1f7d1e8d89e0444cc6248025a31d35d7414aab0e5a78f",
        "lineStart": 120,
        "lineEnd": 120,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md#L120-L120"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4fff060eb23cf1564d17",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Not every alert needs to be tuned or silenced when it's not effective. Some are measuring something worth tracking differently.",
      "headingPath": [
        "When SLOs reduce alert noise",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/guides/when-slos-reduce-alert-noise.md",
