    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ad7c67da9c0e4f79f011",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Label matchers apply to both the alert rule's labels and the labels on its alert instances, so a rule matches when either set of labels satisfies the matcher. For labels whose values are set by Go templates, the matcher runs against the rendered static value, not the template expression, so you can't use a template query to find a match.",
      "headingPath": [
        "View alert rules",
        "Filter and save searches",
        "Search syntax",
        "Match labels with regular expressions"
      ],
      "source": {
