    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0cad568dd9c064163a49",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To collect scraped Alerting metrics, configure Prometheus to scrape metrics from Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 90,
        "lineEnd": 90,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L90-L90"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b70538b67d4fb2192c96",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Grafana ruler, which is responsible for evaluating alert rules, and the Grafana Alertmanager, which is responsible for sending notifications of firing and resolved alerts, provide a number of metrics that let you observe them.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 105,
        "lineEnd": 105,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L105-L105"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fd73285b9c277566a68c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a counter that shows you the number of `normal`, `pending`, `alerting`, `nodata` and `error` alerts. For example, you might want to create an alert that fires when `grafana_alerting_alerts{state=\"error\"}` is greater than 0.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 109,
        "lineEnd": 109,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L109-L109"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7979a33ee306551beb56",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a gauge that shows you the number of alert rules scheduled. An alert rule is scheduled unless it is paused, and the value of this metric should match the total number of non-paused alert rules in Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_schedule_alert_rules"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 113,
        "lineEnd": 113,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L113-L113"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.18aba6f0204799c851c9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a histogram that shows you the time it takes to process an individual tick in the scheduler that evaluates alert rules. If the scheduler takes longer than 10 seconds to process a tick then pending evaluations start to accumulate such that alert rules might later than expected.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_schedule_periodic_duration_seconds_bucket"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 117,
        "lineEnd": 117,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L117-L117"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d459edf302f1bc72c23f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a histogram that shows you how long it takes the scheduler to fetch the latest rules from the database. If this metric is elevated, `schedule_periodic_duration_seconds` is also evaluated.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_schedule_query_alert_rules_duration_seconds_bucket"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 121,
        "lineEnd": 121,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L121-L121"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f98f719e16212f57f69e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a gauge that shows you the number of seconds that the scheduler is behind where it should be. This number increases if `schedule_periodic_duration_seconds` is longer than 10 seconds, and decrease when it is less than 10 seconds. The smallest possible value of this metric is 0.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_scheduler_behind_seconds"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 125,
        "lineEnd": 125,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L125-L125"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.eb95bcfe80f42234d2b9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a histogram that shows you the number of seconds taken to send notifications for firing and resolved alerts. This metric lets you observe slow or over-utilized integrations, such as an SMTP server that is being given emails faster than it can send them.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_notification_latency_seconds_bucket"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 129,
        "lineEnd": 129,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L129-L129"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b0ec3bfcb82eec0fa099",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a counter that shows you the number of failed writes to the configured alert state history backend. It includes a `backend` label to distinguish between different backends (such as `loki` or `prometheus`).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_state_history_writes_failed_total"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 133,
        "lineEnd": 133,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L133-L133"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.16c29cfd69cece9b9699",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, you might want to create an alert that fires when `grafana_alerting_state_history_writes_failed_total{backend=\"prometheus\"}` is greater than 0 to detect when Prometheus remote write is failing.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Grafana-managed alerts",
        "Scraped metrics",
        "grafana_alerting_state_history_writes_failed_total"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
