    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.836fbf167afce98e3c29",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alternatively, you can access the [History page](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/alerting/monitor-status/view-alert-state-history/) in Grafana to visualize and filter state changes for individual alerts or all alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Logs for Grafana-managed alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 168,
        "lineEnd": 168,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L168-L168"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.91f7e15a594358a5c50b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you have enabled notification history, you can also refer to [View notification history](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/alerting/monitor-status/view-notification-history/) to review sent notifications and delivery outcomes in the **History** page **Notifications** tab.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Logs for Grafana-managed alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 170,
        "lineEnd": 170,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L170-L170"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.783bcc17d0f267d8a177",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if you are using Prometheus you should add a `scrape_config` to Prometheus to scrape metrics from your Alertmanager.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Alertmanager"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 184,
        "lineEnd": 184,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L184-L184"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.79fa375cce68c8ef0431",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a counter that shows you the number of invalid alerts that were sent to Alertmanager. This counter should not exceed 0, and so in most cases, create an alert that fires if whenever this metric increases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Alertmanager",
        "alertmanager_alerts",
        "alertmanager_alerts_invalid_total"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 207,
        "lineEnd": 207,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L207-L207"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8940dd3ba577e270a739",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a counter that shows you how many notifications have failed in total. This metric also uses a label \"integration\" to show the number of failed notifications by integration, such as failed emails. In most cases, use the `rate` function to understand how often notifications are failing to be sent.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Alertmanager",
        "alertmanager_alerts",
        "alertmanager_notifications_failed_total"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 215,
        "lineEnd": 215,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L215-L215"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5f8af7f42ac1a4f77776",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a histogram that shows you the amount of time it takes Alertmanager to send notifications and for those notifications to be accepted by the receiving service. This metric uses a label \"integration\" to show the amount of time by integration. For example, you can use this metric to show the 95th percentile latency of sending emails.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Alertmanager",
        "alertmanager_alerts",
        "alertmanager_notification_latency_seconds_bucket"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 219,
        "lineEnd": 219,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L219-L219"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3a3be73bd2989a2a956b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you are using Alertmanager in high availability mode there are a number of additional metrics that you might want to create alerts for.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Alertmanager in high availability mode"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 223,
        "lineEnd": 223,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L223-L223"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e45a24d7cba92d361585",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a gauge that shows you the current number of members in the cluster. The value of this gauge should be the same across all Alertmanagers. If different Alertmanagers are showing different numbers of members then this is indicative of an issue with your Alertmanager cluster. You should look at the metrics and logs from your Alertmanagers to better understand what might be going wrong.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Alertmanager in high availability mode",
        "alertmanager_cluster_members"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 227,
        "lineEnd": 227,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L227-L227"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7feb1c53fcc351ab627b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This metric is a counter that shows you the number of failed peer connection attempts. In most cases you should use the `rate` function to understand how often reconnections fail as this may be indicative of an issue or instability in your network.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Meta monitoring",
        "Metrics for Alertmanager in high availability mode",
        "alertmanager_cluster_members",
        "alertmanager_cluster_reconnections_failed_total"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3c879c1dc4f3b12dcb5b3ee87197aa473b1f67a6",
        "sha256": "623f59558b9afdb079113801301aa4e21d2182a20cbc294775ee1751dd123018",
        "lineStart": 243,
        "lineEnd": 243,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/meta-monitoring.md#L243-L243"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c35038c21fc61bbf7a62",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Alerting supports multi-dimensional alerting, where one alert rule can generate many alerts. For example, you can configure an alert rule to fire an alert every time the CPU of individual virtual machines max out. This topic discusses performance considerations resulting from multi-dimensional alerting.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 23,
        "lineEnd": 23,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L23-L23"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.df8bdd2ed6e8500dabf5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Evaluating alerting rules consumes RAM and CPU to compute the output of an alerting query, and network resources to send alert notifications and write the results to the Grafana SQL database. The configuration of individual alert rules affects the resource consumption and, therefore, the maximum number of rules a given configuration can support.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 25,
        "lineEnd": 25,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L25-L25"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.38f2499e43d544f4d88e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The following section provides a list of alerting performance considerations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 27,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L27-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1c5281c3804c33aa10d1",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Frequency of rule evaluation consideration. The \"Evaluate Every\" property of an alert rule controls the frequency of rule evaluation. It is recommended to use the lowest acceptable evaluation frequency to support more concurrent rules.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 29,
        "lineEnd": 29,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L29-L29"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.167b3dcc41f19efd0fc6",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Cardinality of the rule's result set. For example, suppose you are monitoring API response errors for every API path, on every virtual machine in your fleet. This set has a cardinality of _n_ number of paths multiplied by _v_ number of VMs. You can reduce the cardinality of a result set - perhaps by monitoring errors-per-VM instead of for each path per VM.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 30,
        "lineEnd": 30,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L30-L30"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.801d6924b47b3ae1dab6",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Complexity of the alerting query consideration. Queries that data sources can process and respond to quickly consume fewer resources. Although this consideration is less important than the other considerations listed above, if you have reduced those as much as possible, looking at individual query performance could make a difference.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d74b28dc181d858e1230",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Each evaluation of an alert rule generates a set of alert instances; one for each member of the result set. The state of all the instances is written to the `alert_instance` table in the Grafana SQL database. This number of write-heavy operations can cause issues when using SQLite.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 33,
        "lineEnd": 33,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L33-L33"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e119b9c15762219e1465",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Alerting exposes a metric, `grafana_alerting_rule_evaluations_total` that counts the number of alert rule evaluations. To get a feel for the influence of rule evaluations on your Grafana instance, you can observe the rate of evaluations and compare it with resource consumption. In a Prometheus-compatible database, you can use the query `rate(grafana_alerting_rule_evaluations_total[5m])` to compute the rate over 5 minute windows of time. It's important to remember that this isn't the full picture of rule evaluation. For example, the load is unevenly distributed if you have some rules that evaluate every 10 seconds, and others every 30 minutes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 35,
        "lineEnd": 35,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L35-L35"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e6e758f62e7fa0c339d3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "These factors all affect the load on the Grafana instance, but you should also be aware of the performance impact that evaluating these rules has on your data sources. Alerting queries are often the vast majority of queries handled by monitoring databases, so the same load factors that affect the Grafana instance affect them as well.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L37-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ca9bd5ccd1cc72e103c0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Alerting can retrieve alerting and recording rules **stored** in most available Prometheus, Loki, Mimir, and Alertmanager compatible data sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Limited rule sources support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 41,
        "lineEnd": 41,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L41-L41"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2d74ac790cc5b1aaee9d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "It does not support reading or writing alerting rules from any other data sources but the ones previously mentioned at this time.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Limited rule sources support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 43,
        "lineEnd": 43,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L43-L43"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.839f447408def5ccb4f3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The latest two minor versions of both Prometheus and Alertmanager are supported. We cannot guarantee that older versions work.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Prometheus version support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 47,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L47-L47"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c310edf68306c2325630",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As an example, if the current Prometheus version is `2.31.1`, >= `2.29.0` is supported.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Prometheus version support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.444b1236d4a6e7360c11",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana cannot be used to receive external alerts. You can only send alerts to the Grafana Alertmanager using Grafana managed alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "The Grafana Alertmanager can only receive Grafana managed alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b50dd6acb9ff7a60ae1a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You have the option to send Grafana-managed alerts to an external Alertmanager, you can find this option in the Admin tab on the Alerting page.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "The Grafana Alertmanager can only receive Grafana managed alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 55,
        "lineEnd": 55,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L55-L55"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3279eaeb4d38b8b5ee74",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you have a high number of alert rules or alert instances, the load on the database can get very high.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "High load on database caused by a high number of alert instances"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 61,
        "lineEnd": 61,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L61-L61"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f88ecd305d333e5b4096",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you're upgrading from a Grafana version where you had explicitly disabled `alertingSaveStateCompressed`, enable it and let Grafana run for at least one evaluation cycle _before_ you upgrade to Grafana 13.2 or later. Otherwise, any alert state still held in the old uncompressed format isn't read after the upgrade. This doesn't cause data loss beyond the alert state itself: Grafana re-evaluates every rule and rebuilds instance state from scratch, but you might see a brief, one-time gap in alert history and current state immediately after the upgrade.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "High load on database caused by a high number of alert instances"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 68,
        "lineEnd": 68,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L68-L68"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0e87b6d80873db585ae0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also reduce database load by writing states periodically instead of after every evaluation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "High load on database caused by a high number of alert instances",
        "Save state periodically"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 73,
        "lineEnd": 73,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L73-L73"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.95542d674c578b0c5d4c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Enable the `alertingSaveStatePeriodic` feature toggle to save alert states at the interval specified by `state_periodic_save_interval` instead of after every rule evaluation. Grafana groups all alert instances by rule UID and compresses them together for efficient storage.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "High load on database caused by a high number of alert instances",
        "Save state periodically"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 75,
        "lineEnd": 75,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L75-L75"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.07858d78fee0d9795eee",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, Grafana saves the states every 5 minutes and on each shutdown. Note that `state_periodic_save_batch_size` and `state_periodic_save_jitter_enabled` don't apply here, since Grafana groups instances by rule UID rather than by batch.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "High load on database caused by a high number of alert instances",
        "Save state periodically"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 77,
        "lineEnd": 77,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L77-L77"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9c2134d478a80da7c530",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If Grafana crashes or is force killed, then the database can be up to `state_periodic_save_interval` seconds out of date. When Grafana restarts, the UI might show incorrect state for some alerts until the alerts are re-evaluated. In some cases, alerts that were firing before the crash might fire again. If this happens, Grafana might send duplicate notifications for firing alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "High load on database caused by a high number of alert instances",
        "Save state periodically"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 84,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L84-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2cff02bc7feadb0418f3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Each alert rule evaluation generates one alert instance per series in the rule's query result set. Rules with high-cardinality result sets consume more CPU, memory, network, and database resources, and can produce a large number of alert instances (refer to [High load on database caused by a high number of alert instances](#high-load-on-database-caused-by-a-high-number-of-alert-instances)).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Limit on the number of results per alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 91,
        "lineEnd": 91,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L91-L91"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c06f8e7985d687db597c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To prevent this, Grafana can limit the number of query evaluation results a single alert rule produces in one evaluation. When a rule's query returns more results than the limit, the evaluation fails with an error similar to the following:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Limit on the number of results per alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 93,
        "lineEnd": 93,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L93-L93"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8519da92f0eaa60fd6ba",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The alert rule enters the [Error state](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/nodata-and-error-states/) and produces no alert instances for that evaluation until you reduce its result set below the limit.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Limit on the number of results per alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c46bdb78fe635ffd74e357d5adc97e867aca5f91",
        "sha256": "6d309371de1b629ae548e7951f2b90362472c16411d2ec1de794c69bcb792f22",
        "lineStart": 99,
        "lineEnd": 99,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/index.md#L99-L99"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a529ed076e331d676b56",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In self-managed Grafana, set this limit using the [`alerting_rule_evaluation_results`](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-grafana#alerting_rule_evaluation_results) option in the `[quota]` section. The default is `-1` (unlimited). In Grafana Cloud, Grafana Labs manages this limit.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Performance considerations and limitations",
        "Limit on the number of results per alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
