    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.eda425a8420bca22ae37",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana Cloud, you can use **Infrastructure as code** to declaratively create and manage dashboards via configuration files in source code, and incorporate them efficiently into your own use cases. This enables you to review code, reuse it, and create better workflows. Infrastructure as code tools include Terraform, Ansible, the Grafana Operator, and Grizzly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b26a3a67f6eb5daf314ec05f6c29fac596b3ac82",
        "sha256": "20fb5fd56b56114e0018973b7d395795c4c212cd73c4395ea5ece61167a29125",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/_index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.810f8f2c91010e71d497",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Grafana Cloud, you can use as-code tools to create and manage resources via code, and incorporate them efficiently into your own use cases. This enables you to review code, reuse it, and create better workflows.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 17,
        "lineEnd": 17,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L17-L17"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c5649fad0e3f2c3ff022",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Most of the tools defined here can be used with one another.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 21,
        "lineEnd": 21,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L21-L21"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a125557bdedc05033bc3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana administrators can manage dashboards, alerts and collectors, add synthetic monitoring probes and checks, manage identity and access, and more using the [Terraform provider for Grafana](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/grafana/grafana/latest).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Terraform provider"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 27,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L27-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ec744e0afb896b1952f4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This example dashboard only creates the dashboard and does not add any panels or rows. To get started, see the [Grafana Terraform provider guides](/docs/grafana-cloud/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/terraform/) or refer to the [Terraform Grafana Provider documentation](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/grafana/grafana/latest/docs).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Terraform provider"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 40,
        "lineEnd": 41,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L40-L41"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d51f725b5fefb4fee22",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Terraform provider is best suited for users who are already using Terraform for non-Grafana use cases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Terraform provider",
        "Who is this recommended for?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 45,
        "lineEnd": 45,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L45-L45"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.de0b87c669bbfd42a8ca",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To manage the entire Grafana ecosystem of resources on either Grafana Cloud or OSS deployments of Grafana, it’s best to use the Terraform Grafana provider because it supports the most Grafana resources compared to Grafana’s other as-code solutions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Terraform provider",
        "Who is this recommended for?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 47,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L47-L47"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cd40bc0e536d1c0133f5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For Grafana Fleet Management users, the Grafana Terraform provider is best used to preregister new collectors before they are operational or add remote attributes to collectors already registered with the service.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Terraform provider",
        "Who is this recommended for?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.60a65f3818e2697af6c3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Managing dashboards isn’t the simplest process—you have to work with long JSON files, which can become difficult to review and update, as well. Grafonnet can help with generating dashboard JSONs that can be used in Terraform, but Grafonnet requires knowing Jsonnet.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Terraform provider",
        "Known limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d13ada9636cfd05cf9c8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Resources for configuration management are available for Grafana through the [Ansible collection for Grafana](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/latest/collections/grafana/grafana/index.html#plugins-in-grafana-grafana). The Grafana Ansible collection can be used to manage a variety of resources, including folders, cloud stacks, and dashboards. You can programmatically manage resources on Grafana that aren’t currently part of the Grafana Ansible collection by writing Ansible playbooks that use the HTTP APIs to manage resources for Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Ansible collection"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 57,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L57-L57"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.62b12a40c1d3b147fe11",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This example dashboard creates only the dashboard and does not add any panels or rows.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Ansible collection"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 70,
        "lineEnd": 70,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L70-L70"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.87c85b58797b9096cecb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Like Terraform, the Grafana Ansible collection is best suited for people already using Ansible for non-Grafana use cases. The collection only works for Grafana Cloud right now, so it makes the most sense for Grafana Cloud customers who want to manage resources using Ansible.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Ansible collection",
        "Who is this recommended for?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 76,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L76-L76"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.53e6b871583e50d35984",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Grafana Ansible collection only works for Grafana Cloud and only supports eight resources: API keys, cloud stacks, plugins, dashboards, folders, data sources, alert contact points, and notification policies. This can be a drawback if you want to manage the entire Grafana ecosystem as code with Ansible. As with Terraform, building dashboards is a challenging process.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Ansible collection",
        "Known limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 80,
        "lineEnd": 80,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L80-L80"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e21da4a154f50fafa438",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Grafana Operator is a Kubernetes operator that can provision, manage, and operate Grafana instances and their associated resources within Kubernetes through Custom Resources. This Kubernetes-native tool eases the administration of Grafana, including managing dashboards, data sources, and folders. It also automatically syncs the Kubernetes Custom resources and the actual resources in the Grafana Instance. It supports leveraging Grafonnet for generating Grafana dashboard definitions for seamless dashboard configuration as code.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Operator"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 84,
        "lineEnd": 84,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L84-L84"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0ad4373edb7897809e20",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Teams seeking integrated solutions to manage Grafana resources within the Kubernetes cluster ecosystem.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Operator",
        "Who is this recommended for?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
