    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b4fa09743ce5d1d12532",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Teams employing a GitOps approach, allowing them to treat Grafana configurations as code, stored alongside application manifests for versioned and automated deployments.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Operator",
        "Who is this recommended for?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 113,
        "lineEnd": 113,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L113-L113"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ff11dba05029791291cb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "While the Grafana Operator simplifies many aspects of operating Grafana and its resources on Kubernetes, its current support is mainly focused on managing dashboards, folders, and data sources. Advanced features like alerting and plugins (only works for OSS) are not supported yet.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Operator",
        "Known limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 117,
        "lineEnd": 117,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L117-L117"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3adaa5399f0c08fdd935",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Grafana Crossplane provider](https://github.com/grafana/crossplane-provider-grafana) is built using Terrajet and provides support for all resources supported by the Grafana Terraform provider. It enables users to define Grafana resources as Kubernetes manifests and it also help users who build their GitOps pipelines around Kubernetes manifests using tools like ArgoCD.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Crossplane provider"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 121,
        "lineEnd": 121,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L121-L121"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.29a4ae8076f51b00cc88",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To get started with the Grafana Crossplane provider, install Crossplane in the Kubernetes cluster and use this command to install the provider:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Crossplane provider"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 123,
        "lineEnd": 123,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L123-L123"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.77849867d44f95502bef",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "During installation of the provider, CRDs for all the resources supported by the Terraform provider are added to the cluster so users can begin defining their Grafana resources as Kubernetes custom resources. The Crossplane provider ensures that whatever is defined in the custom resource definitions is what is visible in Grafana UI. If any changes are made directly in the UI, the changes will be discarded when the provider resyncs. This helps ensure that whatever is defined via code in the cluster will be the source of truth for Grafana resources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Crossplane provider"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c976df81106c09ce7ef07752b595b2870128906e",
        "sha256": "3997dbd9cc60d77503d513fb7d8be24d127a45b035709684e39171e69b8589ad",
        "lineStart": 129,
        "lineEnd": 129,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md#L129-L129"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2a5efb30eece4d07f558",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To use the Crossplane provider, you must have the Crossplane CLI and Crossplane installed in the Kubernetes cluster. Note that the Crossplane provider is in an alpha stage, so it has not reached a stable state yet.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana Cloud with Infrastructure as code",
        "Grafana Crossplane provider",
        "Known limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/_index.md",
