    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b334d61e7e52a75b5cbf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This guide covers _secure values_, which you manage with the [`grafana_apps_secret_securevalue_v1beta1`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/grafana/grafana/latest/docs/resources/apps_secret_securevalue_v1beta1) resource. By default, Grafana stores secure values in the built-in _system keeper_, which requires no setup. If you configure an additional keeper and set it as the active keeper for your namespace, Grafana stores new secure values there automatically. For more information, refer to [Activate and use the keeper](#activate-and-use-the-keeper). To store secure values in an external secret manager instead, [provision a keeper](#provision-a-keeper).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Use Terraform to provision secure values"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/terraform/terraform-secrets-management.md",
