      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bdf2576ddc25b01c76aa",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The role name in `assume_role_arn` must be `grafana-secrets-manager`. Grafana can't assume a role with any other name.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Use Terraform to provision secure values",
        "Provision a keeper",
        "Define a keeper"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/terraform/terraform-secrets-management.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "52977e9c09c75dbafbdbbdb7ab05a511e921e281",
        "sha256": "408746cac5de95be048c327c72a92ce56e80f5a9bcb4614d2ab66a4dc946630b",
        "lineStart": 465,
        "lineEnd": 465,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/terraform/terraform-secrets-management.md#L465-L465"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b9722ccf83a0552b2920",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Apply the keeper with the same `terraform apply` workflow you use for a secure value, described in [Provision the secure value with Terraform](#provision-the-secure-value-with-terraform). Unlike a secure value, a keeper has no secret value, so it needs no `ephemeral` variable of its own: `TF_VAR_grafana_auth` for the provider is the only variable you export. Creating a keeper doesn't make it active, so don't create secure values in the same apply until you add the activation resource in [Activate and use the keeper](#activate-and-use-the-keeper) and make new secrets depend on it.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Use Terraform to provision secure values",
        "Provision a keeper",
        "Define a keeper"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/terraform/terraform-secrets-management.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "52977e9c09c75dbafbdbbdb7ab05a511e921e281",
        "sha256": "408746cac5de95be048c327c72a92ce56e80f5a9bcb4614d2ab66a4dc946630b",
        "lineStart": 467,
        "lineEnd": 469,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/infrastructure-as-code/terraform/terraform-secrets-management.md#L467-L469"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.556ddcc54acf10741ad3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The full schema is on the [Terraform Registry](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/grafana/grafana/latest/docs/resources/apps_secret_keeper_v1beta1). The following tables describe the fields you use for a keeper.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Use Terraform to provision secure values",
        "Provision a keeper",
        "Keeper schema reference"
      ],
      "source": {
