        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/foundation-sdk/foundation-sdk-key-concepts.md#L83-L83"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ed142cd5ee7f7ae3db5f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By using option builders, you don't need to manually construct deeply nested configuration objects. Instead, the SDK gives you a typed and guided API that mirrors a dashboards internal structure, making it easier to configure complex options without guesswork or referring back to the JSON schema.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Foundation SDK key concepts",
        "Options"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/foundation-sdk/foundation-sdk-key-concepts.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "eaa8c57d4b329df9800793d1ab7fd9292b6d7c1f",
        "sha256": "f4c2ddb141d117f0422c11c4062709b13f677b0954f0aebb5dfc0bd49403fe1b",
        "lineStart": 103,
        "lineEnd": 103,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/foundation-sdk/foundation-sdk-key-concepts.md#L103-L103"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ac7bc0b9b2b558a1d5ef",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Git Sync in Grafana lets you synchronize your resources so you can store your dashboards as JSON files in any Git provider and manage them as code. You and your team can version control, collaborate, and automate deployments efficiently.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 36,
        "lineEnd": 36,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L36-L36"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.52e787be5a5882436336",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Git Sync functionalities are constantly evolving. [Contact Grafana](https://grafana.com/help/) for support or to report any issues you encounter and help us improve this feature.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 40,
        "lineEnd": 40,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L40-L40"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5a4168d6e22375b7525e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Git Sync allows you to connect external resources with your Grafana instance. After setup, all synchronized resources live in Git under the provisioned folder, and you can continue to have non-provisioned resources outside that folder.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "How it works"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 46,
        "lineEnd": 46,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L46-L46"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a3f66a09b73960ce86a4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Git Sync is bidirectional, so you can modify provisioned resources both from the Grafana UI or from the synced repository, and changes will be reflected in both places.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "How it works"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 48,
        "lineEnd": 48,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L48-L48"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2f131c40ae25531f7426",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Whenever you modify a dashboard directly from the UI, you can also commit those changes to your synchronized Git repositories upon saving. You can configure settings to either enforce PR approvals before merging in your repository, or allow direct commits.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "How it works",
        "Make changes in the Grafana UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 58,
        "lineEnd": 58,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L58-L58"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b302d12eec375ca5afea",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Your Grafana instance polls the provisioned Git resources to synchronize. If you made any changes in your synchronized Git repositories, they will be updated in the Grafana database as well. The Grafana UI reads from the database and updates the UI to reflect these changes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "How it works",
        "Make changes in your Git repositories"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 62,
        "lineEnd": 62,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L62-L62"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.66d81f65bae462531211",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Without webhooks, Grafana polls for changes at the specified interval. The default polling interval is 60 seconds, and you can change this setting in the Grafana UI.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "How it works",
        "Make changes in your Git repositories"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 64,
        "lineEnd": 64,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L64-L64"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.476228f45aaa91fef6c7",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- If you enable the [webhooks feature](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/git-sync-setup/#configure-webhooks-and-image-rendering), repository notifications appear almost immediately.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "How it works",
        "Make changes in your Git repositories"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d7d8a51f2d27da0997ad",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use Git Sync for the following use cases:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 75,
        "lineEnd": 75,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L75-L75"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f78084ba1b5bc0d15ab6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Organizations can maintain a structured, version-controlled history of Grafana dashboards. The version control lets you revert to previous versions when necessary, compare modifications across commits, and ensure transparency in dashboard management.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Version control and auditing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 79,
        "lineEnd": 79,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L79-L79"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.296e4662a7880cb6d780",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Additionally, having a detailed history of changes enhances compliance efforts, as teams can generate audit logs that document who made changes, when they were made, and why.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Version control and auditing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 81,
        "lineEnd": 81,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L81-L81"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a835122cd8c474609c61",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Teams can streamline their workflow by integrating dashboard updates into their CI/CD pipelines. By pushing changes to GitHub, automated processes can trigger validation checks, test dashboard configurations, and deploy updates programmatically using the `gcx` CLI and Foundation SDK.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Automated deployment and CI/CD integration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 85,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L85-L85"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f5b8c6676bfb50e4aadd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Git Sync, multiple users can work on dashboards simultaneously without overwriting each other’s modifications. By leveraging pull requests and branch-based workflows, teams can submit changes for review before merging them into the main branch. This process not only improves quality control but also ensures that dashboards adhere to best practices and organizational standards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Collaborative dashboard development"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 91,
        "lineEnd": 92,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L91-L92"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b84a7838311182ebf52e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Enterprises managing multiple Grafana instances, such as development, staging, and production environments, can seamlessly sync dashboards across these instances. This ensures consistency in visualization and monitoring configurations, reducing discrepancies that might arise from manually managing dashboards in different environments.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Multi-environment synchronization"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 98,
        "lineEnd": 98,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L98-L98"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.87dc3a2361b19737363e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By using Git Sync, teams can automate deployments across environments, eliminating repetitive setup tasks and maintaining a standardized monitoring infrastructure across the organization.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Multi-environment synchronization"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 100,
        "lineEnd": 100,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L100-L100"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.92f296ac348ef9b60c6f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By continuously syncing dashboards to GitHub, organizations can create an always-updated backup, ensuring dashboards are never lost due to accidental deletion or system failures.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Disaster recovery and backup"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 104,
        "lineEnd": 104,
