    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a9cb5071ddf81637a13d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If an issue arises, such as a corrupted dashboard, unintended modification, or a system crash, teams can quickly restore the latest functional version from the Git repository. This not only minimizes downtime but also adds a layer of resilience to Grafana monitoring setups, ensuring critical dashboards remain available when needed.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Common use cases",
        "Disaster recovery and backup"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c16d3bccd4948a117217b85f6ee76c97d112950f",
        "sha256": "be9cfef9c37f98831cdbc1d225e6c3a8d239e5e3276734f848dda44d62ec7c31",
        "lineStart": 106,
        "lineEnd": 106,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md#L106-L106"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ae589c80090f9c0c1794",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Because dashboards are defined in JSON files, you can enable as-code workflows where the JSON file is an output from Go, TypeScript, or another coding language in the format of a dashboard schema.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to Git Sync",
        "Build dashboards as code"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/_index.md",
