    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bfde301b0b441c929ae1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Git Sync registers its own webhooks for each repository connection, so when several Grafana instances sync the same repository, each connection adds to this total. Since [Git providers limit the amount of webhooks](#webhook-limitations-per-provider) you can set for each repository, when the limit is exceeded, your Git provider rejects new webhooks.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up instantaneous pulling and dashboard previews in Pull Requests",
        "Set up webhooks for real-time notification and pull request integration",
        "Webhook limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/git-sync-setup/set-up-extend.md",
