    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.40c31e8bdfbb817e4f8d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Git Sync operations run as jobs. You need the `provisioning.jobs:create` permission to create any job. Moreover, **some job actions are restricted to administrators** and require the `provisioning.repositories:write` permission. This prevents editors from triggering repository-wide operations even though they hold `provisioning.jobs:create`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Git Sync permissions and access control",
        "Configure fine-grained access control (RBAC)",
        "Job actions and required permissions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/git-sync/permissions-grafana.md",
