    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2acd3b3baf6c26d83e66",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Using the `config` and `resources` options, you can migrate Grafana resources from one environment to another, for example, from a development to production environment. The `config` option lets you define the configuration context. Using `resources` with `pull`, `push`, and `serve` lets you pull a defined resource from one instance, and push that resource to another instance. `Serve` allows you to preview changes locally before pushing.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Manage resources with `grafanactl`",
        "Migrate resources between environments"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/as-code/observability-as-code/grafana-cli/grafanactl/grafanacli-workflows.md",
