    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.933cea77afbfbd19196a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Starting from Grafana 9, RBAC has been enabled by default. An option to disable RBAC was introduced as an emergency mechanism and has only been used in rare cases. With Grafana v10 we removed the configuration option to disable RBAC. This ensures that Grafana works consistently across different features and decreases the risk of having issues with Grafana's legacy access control. Additionally, access control for some of the Grafana v10 features only work with the RBAC, so disabling it is no longer an option.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v10.0",
        "General breaking changes",
        "RBAC is on by default in Grafana Enterprise and cannot be disabled",
        "Description"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f55c473a793866712b72c992a0f3e962e71e945b",
        "sha256": "7182bdb5b678e1c91768a46bd37de4cdc244c5408956243298447536324002de",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Breaking changes in Grafana v10.0 > General breaking changes > RBAC is on by default in Grafana Enterprise and cannot be disabled > Description"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.79226427d5b1ed3d4481",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You run Grafana with a Postgres or sqlite database, you import users from different SSO identity providers (like Google and Active Directory), and users who signed in from different providers were previously created twice because of case differences (for example \"<Myra@Grafana.com>\" vs \"<myra@grafana.com>.\"",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v10.0",
        "General breaking changes",
        "Usernames are now case-insensitive by default",
        "You are affected if:"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f55c473a793866712b72c992a0f3e962e71e945b",
        "sha256": "7182bdb5b678e1c91768a46bd37de4cdc244c5408956243298447536324002de",
        "lineStart": 146,
        "lineEnd": 146,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md#L146-L146"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5317bc5c84df4bf69de5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When someone signs up for a Grafana account, they can do it using an email or a login. The fields were case sensitive, which could lead to two or more accounts being created for the same user. Additionally, Grafana allows users to set up an authentication provider, and that provider might return an individual's sign-up email with an uppercased domain name or some combination of uppercase and lowercase letters.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v10.0",
        "General breaking changes",
        "Usernames are now case-insensitive by default",
        "Background"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f55c473a793866712b72c992a0f3e962e71e945b",
        "sha256": "7182bdb5b678e1c91768a46bd37de4cdc244c5408956243298447536324002de",
        "lineStart": 150,
        "lineEnd": 150,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md#L150-L150"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c0a5a1f125317f115a2f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Having several accounts leads to split user permissions, confusion among signup flows, and unused \"zombie\" accounts in your database. Plus, multiple accounts can introduce issues when switching between authentication providers. We refer to these inconsistencies in user uniqueness as a _user identity conflict_.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v10.0",
        "General breaking changes",
        "Usernames are now case-insensitive by default",
        "Background"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f55c473a793866712b72c992a0f3e962e71e945b",
        "sha256": "7182bdb5b678e1c91768a46bd37de4cdc244c5408956243298447536324002de",
        "lineStart": 152,
        "lineEnd": 152,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md#L152-L152"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.22ded74d61c9a02fa72f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana will start matching users without regard for case. Conflicting users will not be able to sign in.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v10.0",
        "General breaking changes",
        "Usernames are now case-insensitive by default",
        "Change in Grafana v10"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f55c473a793866712b72c992a0f3e962e71e945b",
        "sha256": "7182bdb5b678e1c91768a46bd37de4cdc244c5408956243298447536324002de",
        "lineStart": 156,
        "lineEnd": 156,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md#L156-L156"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f8857b6683187fd7cd2c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've built a [CLI tool](https://grafana.com/blog/2022/12/12/guide-to-using-the-new-grafana-cli-user-identity-conflict-tool-in-grafana-9.3/) which users can use to resolve any potential conflicts beforehand. This breaking change was communicated already with Grafana v9.3.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v10.0",
        "General breaking changes",
        "Usernames are now case-insensitive by default",
        "Migration path"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f55c473a793866712b72c992a0f3e962e71e945b",
        "sha256": "7182bdb5b678e1c91768a46bd37de4cdc244c5408956243298447536324002de",
        "lineStart": 160,
        "lineEnd": 160,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v10-0.md#L160-L160"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
