        "lineStart": 66,
        "lineEnd": 66,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v11-0.md#L66-L66"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6cb8138334cf7a76d777",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Refer to this [blog post](https://grafana.com/blog/2024/03/11/removal-of-angularjs-support-in-grafana-what-you-need-to-know/) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v11.0",
        "Users and Operators",
        "AngularJS support is turned off by default",
        "Learn more"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v11-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e65c171b56655c00d5db715c33a93107531034dd",
        "sha256": "be805a73df9178f03227fa8d4cc7ef7fe36a689d21d16d5018ddbb637fc85dc0",
        "lineStart": 70,
        "lineEnd": 70,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v11-0.md#L70-L70"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5ce63a3c8a5cb6907b55",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Effective starting in Grafana v11, anonymous users are counted and charged as users in Grafana Enterprise. When you upgrade to v11, anonymous users will be automatically counted as active users against your Grafana Enterprise license.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v11.0",
        "Users and Operators",
        "Grafana Enterprise: Anonymous devices are billed as users",
        "Description"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v11-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e65c171b56655c00d5db715c33a93107531034dd",
        "sha256": "be805a73df9178f03227fa8d4cc7ef7fe36a689d21d16d5018ddbb637fc85dc0",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 76,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v11-0.md#L76-L76"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Breaking changes in Grafana v11.0 > Users and Operators > Grafana Enterprise: Anonymous devices are billed as users > Description"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b05e1a23fdee0ee02bb8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Turn off anonymous access, and consider using public dashboards to allow view-only access to publicly-accessible dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v11.0",
        "Users and Operators",
        "Grafana Enterprise: Anonymous devices are billed as users",
        "Migration/mitigation"
      ],
