    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a5032661212d4f3133de",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Legacy alerting has reached its end-of-life. In Grafana v11 you can no longer enable legacy alerting, and Grafana will fail to start if the settings are not updated to run the new Grafana Alerting. This also means that starting in Grafana v11, it is no longer possible to migrate from legacy alerting to our new alerting. Grafana v10.4.x is the last version that offers migration, so make sure to migrate to the new Grafana Alerting system _before_ upgrading to Grafana v11. Learn more about Grafana Alerting and the advantages of the new system in the [legacy alerting deprecation documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/v10.4/alerting/set-up/migrating-alerts/legacy-alerting-deprecation/). Learn more about migration in the [upgrade alerting documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/v10.4/alerting/set-up/migrating-alerts/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Breaking changes in Grafana v11.0",
        "Users and Operators",
        "Legacy alerting is entirely removed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/breaking-changes/breaking-changes-v11-0.md",
