    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a551f65ebdf2665d3348",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Annotations](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/build-dashboards/annotate-visualizations/) overlay rich event information on top of graphs. With the Amazon CloudWatch data source, annotations are based on [CloudWatch alarm history](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/AlarmThatSendsEmail.html). Each alarm history item within the dashboard time range—such as a state change, configuration update, or action—becomes an annotation, so you can correlate alarm activity with the rest of your dashboard data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/annotations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "567430df82cce90bd65234bc648ec20c7bf15365",
