    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4889978b7f1c4e160eab",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Unlike data sources that build annotations from free-form queries, CloudWatch annotations query existing CloudWatch alarms and return their state-change history. Grafana finds the matching alarms using one of two methods, retrieves each alarm's history with `cloudwatch:DescribeAlarmHistory`, and renders every history item as an annotation:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch annotations",
        "How CloudWatch annotations work"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/annotations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "567430df82cce90bd65234bc648ec20c7bf15365",
        "sha256": "1134e2a7951e46d97473a1667a2e1d8db7a21a2b1961bf20a83c831fed62d980",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/annotations/index.md#L37-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.167ba5700efa4d545848",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Match alarms by metric:** Grafana calls `cloudwatch:DescribeAlarmsForMetric` to find alarms attached to a specific metric.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch annotations",
        "How CloudWatch annotations work"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/annotations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "567430df82cce90bd65234bc648ec20c7bf15365",
        "sha256": "1134e2a7951e46d97473a1667a2e1d8db7a21a2b1961bf20a83c831fed62d980",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/annotations/index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4e361267c4c370cbbe54",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Match alarms by prefix:** Grafana calls `cloudwatch:DescribeAlarms` with your alarm name and action prefixes, so AWS returns only alarms whose names and actions start with those prefixes. Grafana then filters the returned alarms by the namespace, metric name, dimensions, statistic, and period you specify.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch annotations",
        "How CloudWatch annotations work"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/annotations/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "567430df82cce90bd65234bc648ec20c7bf15365",
        "sha256": "1134e2a7951e46d97473a1667a2e1d8db7a21a2b1961bf20a83c831fed62d980",
        "lineStart": 40,
        "lineEnd": 40,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/annotations/index.md#L40-L40"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e5a8f5f6cc0f446728c5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Each annotation includes the alarm name as its title, the alarm history item type as a tag (for example, `StateUpdate`, `ConfigurationUpdate`, or `Action`), and the history summary as its text.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch annotations",
        "How CloudWatch annotations work"
      ],
      "source": {
