    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8fe734a6538dcffc55f9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This method reads the AWS shared credentials file for a specified profile. Unlike `AWS SDK Default` which also reads the shared credentials file, this option lets you specify a profile directly without environment variables. This option provides no fallback to other credential providers and fails if the file credentials are invalid.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Select an authentication method"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L47-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d5a6f990413a9683466e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- `Access & secret key` corresponds to the [StaticProvider](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-go/api/aws/credentials/#StaticProvider) and authenticates using a specified access key ID and secret key pair.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Select an authentication method"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7276a5cb0c4a25fb143e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This method doesn't provide fallback authentication and fails if the key pair is invalid. It's available in Grafana Cloud, though `Grafana Assume Role` is recommended there because it avoids managing long-term access keys.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Select an authentication method"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2d8f819b4f4e3a63238d",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- `Grafana Assume Role` - With this authentication method, Grafana Cloud users create an AWS IAM role that has a trust relationship with the Grafana AWS account. Grafana uses [STS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/welcome.html) to generate temporary credentials on its behalf. This method eliminates the need to generate secret and access keys for users. Refer to [Use Grafana Assume Role](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/#use-grafana-assume-role) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Select an authentication method"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 52,
        "lineEnd": 52,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L52-L52"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.952cdff98ac95c25e354",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- `Workspace IAM Role` corresponds to the [EC2RoleProvider](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-go/api/aws/credentials/ec2rolecreds/#EC2RoleProvider).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Select an authentication method"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4ca5864f72bba9d4afeb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The EC2RoleProvider retrieves credentials from a role attached to the EC2 instance running Grafana. While AWS SDK Default can achieve similar results, this option provides no fallback authentication. Amazon Managed Grafana enables this option by default.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Select an authentication method"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 54,
        "lineEnd": 55,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L54-L55"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c76d052cac9f72340ce",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you configure **Assume Role ARN**, Grafana uses the provided credentials to perform an [sts:AssumeRole](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/API_AssumeRole.html) call. The primary authentication method only needs permission to assume the role, while the assumed role requires CloudWatch access permissions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Assume a role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 61,
        "lineEnd": 61,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L61-L61"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.da435b4028fe72f6da8e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, you might use one set of long-term credentials across all AWS data sources but want to limit each data source's AWS access (such as separating staging and production data access). You could create separate credentials for each data source with distinct permissions, but this approach requires managing and rotating multiple secret and access keys across many data source instances.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Assume a role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 63,
        "lineEnd": 63,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L63-L63"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0841ea3d295ad3753533",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Instead, assume role functionality lets you use one set of AWS credentials across all AWS data sources with a single permission: the ability to assume roles through STS. You then create separate IAM roles for each data source that specify temporary permissions. Since IAM roles are not credentials, they require no rotation and simplify management.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Assume a role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6596779925b08cf43bd8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If the **Assume Role ARN** field is left empty, Grafana uses the provided credentials from the selected authentication method directly, and permissions to AWS data must be attached directly to those credentials. The **Assume Role ARN** field is optional for all authentication methods except for Grafana Assume Role.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Assume a role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 67,
        "lineEnd": 67,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L67-L67"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.067f594f20a71ad791af",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To disable this feature in open source Grafana or Grafana Enterprise, refer to [`assume_role_enabled`](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#assume_role_enabled).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Assume a role"
      ],
      "source": {
