    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d07681d3bffce7727489",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Create a file at `~/.aws/credentials`, the `HOME` path for the user running the `grafana-server` service.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use an AWS credentials file"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 89,
        "lineEnd": 89,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L89-L89"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.eeb8caa36bad66d052fe",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If the credentials file appears to be in the correct location but isn't working, move your `aws` file to `/usr/share/grafana/` and set the credentials file permissions to `0644`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use an AWS credentials file"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 92,
        "lineEnd": 92,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L92-L92"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.52392b2b9fcbae67bcec",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "EKS IAM roles for service accounts (IRSA) are an AWS EKS feature that allows pods to assume IAM roles without storing long-term credentials. When you configure IRSA in your EKS cluster, AWS injects temporary credentials into your pod as projected volume mounts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use EKS IAM roles for service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 106,
        "lineEnd": 106,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L106-L106"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e671740e88db51356adc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana containers, the process runs as user `472` (`grafana`). By default, Kubernetes mounts the projected credentials with permissions for the root user only.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use EKS IAM roles for service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 108,
        "lineEnd": 109,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L108-L109"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a91650f37545e01ee257",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To grant user `472` permission to access the credentials, and prevent fallback to the IAM role attached to the EC2 instance, set a [security context](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/security-context/) for your pod.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use EKS IAM roles for service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 111,
        "lineEnd": 111,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L111-L111"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a912253f22e46709fb52",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Assume Role is available only in Grafana Cloud. It's currently supported only for the Amazon CloudWatch and Amazon Athena data sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use Grafana Assume Role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 125,
        "lineEnd": 125,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L125-L125"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "conditional-or-paid-restriction-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.aa39f964e7d71a478190",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Grafana Assume Role authentication provider lets you access AWS without creating or managing long-term AWS IAM users or rotating access keys. Instead, you can create an IAM role that has permissions to access CloudWatch and trusts a Grafana AWS account.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use Grafana Assume Role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 128,
        "lineEnd": 128,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L128-L128"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.909faba57e3bab850169",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Grafana AWS account then makes a Security Token Service (STS) request to generate temporary credentials for your AWS data. This request includes an `externalID` unique to your Grafana Cloud account, which ensures users can access only their own AWS resources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use Grafana Assume Role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 130,
        "lineEnd": 130,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L130-L130"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.80e210355e7f7cca8fc6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The trust policy names the shared Grafana AWS account as the trusted principal, but this doesn't grant every Grafana customer access to your role. The `sts:ExternalId` condition restricts the trust to your unique external ID, so AWS only allows an assume-role request that presents that exact value. Grafana sends your external ID only for your own data source requests. The external ID isn't a secret, but combined with the account-level trust it ensures one customer can't assume another customer's role. Keep the `sts:ExternalId` condition in the trust policy — removing it would let any account that Grafana trusts assume your role.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure AWS authentication",
        "Use Grafana Assume Role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2d131f34bdc1a2a0359d49e541ce35ce201cd154",
        "sha256": "84d1e043399ac35275e14ad5a6231a0692fa35043d31b823508f48d6c0993d0a",
        "lineStart": 133,
        "lineEnd": 133,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/aws-authentication/index.md#L133-L133"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.034dbcfe102a50a652b9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
