    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5bc55c944eba59faed45",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| **Statistic**   | Choose how to aggregate your data. Options are `Average`, `Maximum`, `Minimum`, `Sum`, `SampleCount`, and `IQM`. You can also enter a custom value, such as a percentile like `p99`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "CloudWatch Metrics query editor components"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 62,
        "lineEnd": 62,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L62-L62"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0bc802f8b1e185ed8674",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| **Dimensions**  | Select dimensions from the drop-down. Examples: `InstanceId`, `FunctionName`, `latency`. You can add several dimensions to your query.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "CloudWatch Metrics query editor components"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 63,
        "lineEnd": 63,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L63-L63"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0aad0b9c6a42dfe61793",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| **Match exact** | _Optional_. When enabled, this option restricts query results to metrics that precisely match the specified dimensions and their values. All dimensions of the queried metric must be explicitly defined in the query to ensure an exact schema match. If disabled, the query will also return metrics that match the defined schema but possess additional dimensions.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "CloudWatch Metrics query editor components"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 64,
        "lineEnd": 64,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L64-L64"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7ec5cc4323af928a433a",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| **ID**          | _Optional_. Unique identifier required by the GetMetricData API for referencing queries in math expressions. Must start with a lowercase letter and can include letters, numbers, and underscores. If not specified, Grafana generates an ID using the pattern `query[refId]` (for example, `queryA`for the first query row).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "CloudWatch Metrics query editor components"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.615e80dc910ccc9911a0",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| **Period**      | The minimum time interval, in seconds, between data points. The default is `auto`. CloudWatch accepts periods of 1, 5, 10, 30, or any multiple of 60 seconds. When set to `auto` or left blank, Grafana calculates the period by dividing the time range in seconds by 2000, then rounding up to the next value among 60, 300, 900, 3600, 21600, and 86400. The available periods depend on the age of the data: because CloudWatch stores older metrics at a lower resolution under its [retention policy](https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2016/11/cloudwatch-extends-metrics-retention-and-new-user-interface/), the shorter periods aren't available for older time ranges. |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "CloudWatch Metrics query editor components"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 66,
        "lineEnd": 66,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L66-L66"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.809da3793d82ec9790db",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| **Label**       | _Optional_. Add a customized time series legend name. The label field overrides the default metric legend name using CloudWatch dynamic labels. Time-based dynamic labels like ${MIN_MAX_TIME_RANGE} derive legend values from the current timezone in the time range picker. For the full list of label patterns and limitations, refer to [CloudWatch dynamic labels](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/graph-dynamic-labels.html).                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "CloudWatch Metrics query editor components"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
