    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.636e4679dc85a964e331",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The query returns the average CPU utilization for all EC2 instances in the default region. With `Match Exact` disabled and `InstanceId` using a wildcard, the query retrieves metrics for any EC2 instance regardless of additional dimensions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Create dynamic queries with dimension wildcards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 137,
        "lineEnd": 137,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L137-L137"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8230af19e9c58558b960",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Auto-scaling events add new instances to the graph without manual instance ID tracking. As with other metric search queries, AWS returns up to 100 metrics per `GetMetricData` request.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Create dynamic queries with dimension wildcards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 139,
        "lineEnd": 139,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L139-L139"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c145e098824efa790852",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Click the [**Query inspector**](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/#navigate-the-query-editor) button and select **Meta Data** to see the search expression that's automatically built to support wildcards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Create dynamic queries with dimension wildcards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 141,
        "lineEnd": 141,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L141-L141"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.de882fa28217c577bb1c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To learn more about search expressions, refer to the [CloudWatch documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/search-expression-syntax.html). The search expression is defined by default in such a way that the queried metrics must match the defined dimension names exactly. This means that in the example, the query returns only metrics with exactly one dimension containing the name `InstanceId`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Create dynamic queries with dimension wildcards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 143,
        "lineEnd": 145,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L143-L145"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e84dcee5e9260017f683",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Disabling `Match Exact` includes metrics with additional dimensions and creates a search expression even without wildcards. Grafana searches for any metric matching at least the namespace, metric name, and all defined dimensions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Create dynamic queries with dimension wildcards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 149,
        "lineEnd": 149,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L149-L149"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.111d1ee91c39d50ed9e5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When defining dimension values based on multi-valued template variables, the data source uses a search expression to query for the matching metrics. This enables the use of multiple template variables in one query, and also lets you use template variables for queries that have the `Match Exact` option disabled.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Use multi-value template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 154,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L153-L154"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1c08a18e5f3e564fc69b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Search expressions are limited to 1,024 characters, so your query might fail if you have a long list of values. We recommend using the asterisk (`*`) wildcard instead of the `All` option to query all metrics that have any value for a certain dimension name.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Use multi-value template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 156,
        "lineEnd": 157,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L156-L157"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.febbfc269ba4e74126be",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Multi-valued template variables are supported only for dimension values. Using multi-valued template variables for `Region`, `Namespace`, or `Metric Name` is not supported.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Use multi-value template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
