    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a108ca1269c876ba4470",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you use the expression field to reference another query, such as `queryA * 2`, you can't create an alert rule based on that query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Metric Search queries",
        "Use metric math expressions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 169,
        "lineEnd": 169,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L169-L169"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2cbd69b153393664ab90",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you select `Builder` mode within the Metric search editor, a new Account field is displayed. Use the `Account` field to specify which of the linked monitoring accounts to target for the given query. By default, the `All` option is specified, which will target all linked accounts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Query metrics across AWS monitoring accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 174,
        "lineEnd": 174,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L174-L174"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9c4b905f5c3a6bc8f51a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "While in `Code` mode, you can specify any math expression. If the Monitoring account badge displays in the query editor header, all `SEARCH` expressions entered in this field will be cross-account by default and can query metrics from linked accounts. Note that while queries run cross-account, the autocomplete feature currently doesn't fetch cross-account resources, so you'll need to manually specify resource names when writing cross-account queries. You can limit the search to one or a set of accounts, as documented in the [AWS documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-Unified-Cross-Account.html).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Query metrics across AWS monitoring accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 176,
        "lineEnd": 177,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L176-L177"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9917ee574173c90692a4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you use a CloudWatch [`SEARCH`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/search-expression-syntax.html) expression, consider using the `$__period_auto` macro rather than specifying a period explicitly. The `$__period_auto` macro will resolve to a [CloudWatch period](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/APIReference/API_GetMetricData.html) that is suitable for the chosen time range.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Period macro"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 181,
        "lineEnd": 181,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L181-L181"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.eb6fc1cbe42688a28c9e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Left-clicking a time series in the panel displays a context menu with a link to `View in CloudWatch console`. Clicking the link opens a new tab that takes you to the CloudWatch console and displays all metrics for that query. If you're not logged in to the CloudWatch console, the link forwards you to the login page. The link provided is valid for any account but displays the expected metrics only if you're logged in to the account that corresponds to the selected data source in Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch query editor",
        "Query CloudWatch metrics",
        "Deep-link Grafana panels to the CloudWatch console"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ef7df40715eb7f51a378b68c41c217a24bf2e54e",
        "sha256": "2fe99ed2b68f84a70ad35679bb7e67dc68175a40df0b6cabd0948aff1ccd7f23",
        "lineStart": 185,
        "lineEnd": 188,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/index.md#L185-L188"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
