    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.59c9dbcd9778355947ad",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When cross-account observability is enabled, the **Metrics**, **Dimension Keys**, **Dimension Values**, and **Log Groups** query types also show an optional **Account** field. Use it to target a specific linked monitoring account, or leave it unset to query all linked accounts. For more information, refer to [Cross-account observability](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/query-editor/#cross-account-observability).",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Use query variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "222dc4971129c157ad39debc1f66654d0836e939",
        "sha256": "3736473adf59d23b5a128769666f6734318019c3c336d4d6186761652b270eb4",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b5c986f15ef3d83dc6b4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For details about the metrics CloudWatch provides, refer to the [CloudWatch documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/DeveloperGuide/CW_Support_For_AWS.html).",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Use query variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "222dc4971129c157ad39debc1f66654d0836e939",
        "sha256": "3736473adf59d23b5a128769666f6734318019c3c336d4d6186761652b270eb4",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b6d28835271001db201a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use the Grafana variable syntax to include variables in queries. A query variable dynamically retrieves values from your data source using a query. For details, refer to the [variable syntax documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/variable-syntax/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Use query variables",
        "Use variables in queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "222dc4971129c157ad39debc1f66654d0836e939",
        "sha256": "3736473adf59d23b5a128769666f6734318019c3c336d4d6186761652b270eb4",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 58,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md#L57-L58"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b4be39aa326429cf57b4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "CloudWatch metric queries support variables in the **Region**, **Namespace**, **Metric name**, dimension key, and dimension value fields.",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Use query variables",
        "Use variables in queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "222dc4971129c157ad39debc1f66654d0836e939",
        "sha256": "3736473adf59d23b5a128769666f6734318019c3c336d4d6186761652b270eb4",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.51b3749541e706da885c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if you create a variable named `region` with the **Regions** query type and a variable named `instance` with the **EC2 Instance Attributes** query type, you can reference them in a metric query by setting the query editor **Region** to `$region` and a dimension value to `$instance`. The dashboard then updates as you change the selected region and instance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Use query variables",
        "Use variables in queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "222dc4971129c157ad39debc1f66654d0836e939",
