    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.067dac883dae5d56c961",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The earlier `ec2_instance_attribute(region, attributeName, filters)` query syntax is still supported. Grafana automatically migrates existing variables that use it to the EC2 Instance Attributes query type.",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Query EC2 instance attributes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "222dc4971129c157ad39debc1f66654d0836e939",
        "sha256": "3736473adf59d23b5a128769666f6734318019c3c336d4d6186761652b270eb4",
        "lineStart": 73,
        "lineEnd": 73,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md#L73-L73"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.be14255f469ddd1e68d5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Each filter has a key and a comma-separated list of matching values. Use the [filters supported by `ec2:DescribeInstances`](http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_DescribeInstances.html), such as instance properties. To filter by tag, use a key in the form `tag:<name>`, for example `tag:Environment`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Query EC2 instance attributes",
        "Filters"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "222dc4971129c157ad39debc1f66654d0836e939",
        "sha256": "3736473adf59d23b5a128769666f6734318019c3c336d4d6186761652b270eb4",
        "lineStart": 78,
        "lineEnd": 78,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md#L78-L78"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1abc65ab93f56838926e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A query returns one attribute per instance. You can select any attribute that has a single value and isn't an object or array, also known as a flat attribute. These attributes mirror the fields of the AWS EC2 [`Instance`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_Instance.html) object, where you can find a definition of each one. Because the available attributes track the AWS API, the following list might not be exhaustive:",
      "headingPath": [
        "CloudWatch template variables",
        "Query EC2 instance attributes",
        "Select attributes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/aws-cloudwatch/template-variables/index.md",
