      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.94fef25ce9ce6fcf6b7c",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| `$__escapeMulti($myVar)`        | Escapes illegal characters in multi-value template variables. If `$myVar` has the values `'\\\\grafana-vm\\Network(eth0)\\Total','\\\\hello!'` as a string, use this to expand it to `@'\\\\grafana-vm\\Network(eth0)\\Total', @'\\\\hello!'`. If using single-value variables, escape the variable inline instead: `@'\\$myVar'`.                                                                                                                                                          |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Azure Monitor query editor",
        "Query Azure Monitor Logs",
        "Use macros in Logs queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/azure-monitor/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7e9d70541f1e4e273a619ba9e62b5958327ea3ee",
        "sha256": "06c986577af5c0ca3965b3815e378dc6ecf5d82a71accceca9354c5baeafb011",
        "lineStart": 298,
        "lineEnd": 298,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/azure-monitor/query-editor/index.md#L298-L298"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0fd9210f3e5039f78c6c",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| `$__contains(colName, $myVar)`  | Expands multi-value template variables. If `$myVar` has the value `'value1','value2'`, use this to expand it to `colName in ('value1','value2')`. If using the `All` option, check the `Include All Option` checkbox, and type the value `all` in the `Custom all value` field. If `$myVar` has the value `all`, the macro instead expands to `1 == 1`. For template variables with many options, this avoids building a large \"where..in\" clause, which improves performance. |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Azure Monitor query editor",
        "Query Azure Monitor Logs",
        "Use macros in Logs queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/azure-monitor/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7e9d70541f1e4e273a619ba9e62b5958327ea3ee",
        "sha256": "06c986577af5c0ca3965b3815e378dc6ecf5d82a71accceca9354c5baeafb011",
        "lineStart": 299,
        "lineEnd": 299,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/azure-monitor/query-editor/index.md#L299-L299"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c34f08b261890a73b21",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Additionally, Grafana has the built-in [`$__interval` macro](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/#query-options), which calculates an interval in seconds.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Azure Monitor query editor",
        "Query Azure Monitor Logs",
        "Use macros in Logs queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/azure-monitor/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7e9d70541f1e4e273a619ba9e62b5958327ea3ee",
        "sha256": "06c986577af5c0ca3965b3815e378dc6ecf5d82a71accceca9354c5baeafb011",
        "lineStart": 301,
        "lineEnd": 301,
